WEBVTT

01:05.074 --> 01:06.438
Look, I told you what happens

01:06.572 --> 01:07.600
when the neck
don't break straight away

01:07.736 --> 01:09.170
and they get strangled. Look.

01:10.774 --> 01:11.976
He's got a stiffy.

01:12.111 --> 01:14.578
Shh! You dirty boys.

01:16.215 --> 01:17.817
Wait for it.

01:33.068 --> 01:35.328
It's fucking Hanging Day!

01:37.804 --> 01:40.339
Yeah!

01:50.346 --> 01:53.155
Sinner!

01:53.655 --> 01:54.620
Zillah!

01:54.755 --> 01:55.981
Yeah!

02:05.128 --> 02:06.167
Yes!

02:09.164 --> 02:11.766
Sinners.
Come get your sinners.

02:11.900 --> 02:13.200
Ha'penny for a sinner.

02:21.508 --> 02:22.475
Keep up.

02:25.155 --> 02:26.684
Keep up.

02:34.626 --> 02:36.428
-You're hurting me.
-Come on!

03:30.343 --> 03:32.577
You wanted to know
why he was hanged.

03:34.391 --> 03:36.147
It's not my fault
men are disgusting.

03:36.282 --> 03:37.517
Well, you shouldn't
have told me

03:37.653 --> 03:38.623
no matter what I said.

03:39.758 --> 03:43.560
Poor dolly.
Oh, I'm going to die.

03:43.695 --> 03:46.229
If you are,
then be quick about it,

03:46.364 --> 03:47.295
for I have things to do.

03:47.432 --> 03:49.737
What a frightful racket.

03:49.872 --> 03:51.799
Papa!

03:51.935 --> 03:54.403
Oh, you look like a plate
of corned beef.

03:54.537 --> 03:55.705
Have you been crying?

03:56.540 --> 03:58.104
No. Only racing.

03:58.240 --> 04:00.344
Racing?
If your mother were still here

04:00.480 --> 04:01.743
she'd batter me
around the head

04:01.879 --> 04:03.147
to see
how I've let you run wild.

04:03.282 --> 04:04.614
She would not.

04:04.751 --> 04:06.019
Oh, you didn't know her.
She was a terror.

04:06.154 --> 04:07.116
She boxed for the county.

04:08.753 --> 04:10.754
She had hands
like meat plates.

04:10.891 --> 04:13.460
And her mustache was
as big and bristly as a broom.

04:14.522 --> 04:15.757
No.

04:15.892 --> 04:17.165
I expect
you shall have one too, Cathy,

04:17.300 --> 04:18.926
since they run
in the maternal line.

04:19.062 --> 04:22.931
Stop! You must not talk
about Mama like that.

04:23.065 --> 04:27.232
And I shall not have
a mustache. I shall not!

04:28.441 --> 04:30.477
Don't be tiresome, Cathy.

04:30.611 --> 04:33.639
Nobody likes a sourpuss.
As well as a fright.

04:33.775 --> 04:35.105
God's teeth, Nelly.

04:35.240 --> 04:36.181
Can you do something
about her?

04:36.317 --> 04:37.377
That's what you're here for.

04:37.512 --> 04:38.914
Yes, sir.

04:39.048 --> 04:40.813
And tell Mrs. Burton
I shall dine at The Ram.

04:40.948 --> 04:42.655
Oh, do not go, Papa. Please!

04:42.792 --> 04:44.622
I shall go because the company
is much better at The Ram

04:44.758 --> 04:47.459
and there is considerably
less weeping.

04:47.594 --> 04:49.721
Now then,
where's my fucking horse?

04:49.856 --> 04:51.866
I'll warn the maids.

05:04.311 --> 05:08.415
Papa! I'm sorry! Papa!

05:13.689 --> 05:15.918
Get up! Get a move on!

05:28.527 --> 05:31.230
See it were hotpot
at The Ram again, Zillah.

05:31.366 --> 05:33.738
I'm amazed
he managed to eat anything.

05:33.874 --> 05:36.606
Oh. He's pissed up the wall
again, Mrs. Burton.

05:36.741 --> 05:38.973
Right.
You know what that means.

05:40.746 --> 05:42.384
Check his britches
for soiling.

05:44.648 --> 05:46.178
That poor little girl.

05:49.723 --> 05:52.049
And what of that thing
he brought home, eh?

05:52.185 --> 05:54.055
It's hiding somewhere.

05:54.189 --> 05:56.123
But what's it doing here?

05:56.258 --> 05:58.631
Mr. Earnshaw had
one of his fits of charity.

05:58.765 --> 06:03.262
Oh, Lord. Then pray
for that little sod too.

06:12.210 --> 06:13.513
Hello?

06:31.200 --> 06:32.467
What are you--

06:43.405 --> 06:45.308
 And I said,
 "This is not Liverpool,

06:45.444 --> 06:46.809
this is not Bristol.

06:46.944 --> 06:49.679
You cannot kick a child
in the street."

06:49.815 --> 06:51.551
And the poor
wretch's father...

06:52.851 --> 06:54.417
Well, it's probably
his father...

06:54.552 --> 06:56.247
Anyway, the man said,

06:56.382 --> 06:57.586
"Well, you take
the little devil then

06:57.720 --> 06:59.052
if you're so worried."

06:59.189 --> 07:02.023
And I said,
"Well, I shall! I shall!"

07:03.229 --> 07:04.763
And here we are.

07:08.966 --> 07:11.330
I was only asking
how long it is

07:11.464 --> 07:13.837
you intend us to feed
and clothe him, sir.

07:13.972 --> 07:15.233
As it will affect
the household purse.

07:15.367 --> 07:16.807
I intend him to be clothed
and fed

07:16.941 --> 07:19.478
for as long as I intend it!

07:19.613 --> 07:22.143
Why must I be surrounded
by women?

07:22.280 --> 07:25.315
Spend my days being endlessly
badgered and sniped.

07:25.450 --> 07:26.951
Papa!

07:27.085 --> 07:29.656
Oh, here's another hellcat
sent to torment me.

07:29.793 --> 07:32.059
Oh, there is not a better
father in all the world.

07:32.193 --> 07:34.021
Nor a better man.

07:34.156 --> 07:36.527
Oh, so you like
your new friend, do you?

07:36.663 --> 07:39.631
Very much, Papa.
Very, very much.

07:39.766 --> 07:42.469
Although I do not think
he can talk,

07:42.603 --> 07:44.398
therefore cannot give me
his name.

07:44.532 --> 07:48.465
So I've called him Heathcliff,
after my dead brother.

07:50.641 --> 07:51.678
Heathcliff...

07:54.682 --> 07:58.113
Heathcliff, come here,
my dear boy.

07:59.485 --> 08:01.347
Come, come, come.

08:08.224 --> 08:10.658
You are most heartily
welcome here.

08:10.795 --> 08:11.824
- Oh!
- Oh!

08:11.959 --> 08:13.665
Can I dress him up?

08:13.801 --> 08:15.866
Yes, of course.
He shall be your pet.

08:17.703 --> 08:20.498
I shall be very, very kind.

08:20.634 --> 08:24.006
Unless you're bad,
and then I shall pinch you.

08:26.814 --> 08:29.845
Die, die, die!

08:29.981 --> 08:32.713
Kill that rat!
Get him in the eye.

08:32.849 --> 08:34.213
Get him in the eye. Go on!

08:34.348 --> 08:36.886
Nice for her to have a friend.

08:37.021 --> 08:39.517
A real friend, I mean.
Not a paid one.

08:41.523 --> 08:45.428
Companions aren't paid.
Companions are ladies, Zillah.

08:47.868 --> 08:49.663
Just because
your father was a lord

08:49.800 --> 08:51.902
doesn't make you a lady.

08:52.037 --> 08:54.871
Bastards can't be ladies,
Miss Nelly.

08:55.007 --> 08:56.771
No matter
how much their father paid

08:56.906 --> 08:58.436
to have them hidden away.

09:26.742 --> 09:31.441
"Puh...
Puh-on-e-yuh. Puh-on"...

09:31.578 --> 09:33.741
Po-ny. The pony.

09:37.276 --> 09:39.082
"The pony"...

09:39.216 --> 09:43.217
"The pony a... a-tuh-eh"...

09:43.352 --> 09:46.960
Ate! The pony ate!
The pony ate the grass.

09:47.097 --> 09:49.796
There's a picture, Heathcliff.
There's a picture of it, look!

09:49.930 --> 09:52.090
Honestly, I shall have to make
you a paper cone

09:52.224 --> 09:53.832
and call you a dunce.

09:53.968 --> 09:55.767
And if you do,
I'll throw you out the window

09:55.903 --> 09:58.002
and let the birds peck
at your eyes!

09:58.137 --> 10:01.336
I'm not doing it anymore.
I don't wanna read!

10:01.472 --> 10:03.133
- Temper, temper.
- Shut up.

10:13.385 --> 10:14.480
Sorry.

10:17.689 --> 10:19.187
Sorry, Heathcliff.

10:22.063 --> 10:23.894
Do you want to try again?
I'll be more patient,

10:24.028 --> 10:25.558
- I promise.
- No.

10:25.692 --> 10:26.829
Well, then you shall
never read and never advance

10:26.963 --> 10:27.928
and be very stupid forever!

10:28.062 --> 10:30.297
-Go away.
-No.

10:31.263 --> 10:32.999
-Go away.
-No.

10:33.135 --> 10:34.802
-Just go away!
-No.

10:34.938 --> 10:37.310
-Go away!
-No!

10:42.174 --> 10:43.607
I won't go away.

10:47.213 --> 10:48.249
I'll never go away.

10:50.652 --> 10:53.321
I will never leave you
no matter what you do.

11:23.482 --> 11:25.518
Walk up. That's it.

11:50.079 --> 11:52.381
Cathy, can I come?

11:52.518 --> 11:55.086
No, no, you wouldn't like it.
You're far too sensible.

11:59.122 --> 12:01.388
Come on. She might follow us.

12:21.575 --> 12:22.977
I'm the queen of the castle,

12:23.113 --> 12:25.380
and you're the dirty rascal.

12:26.412 --> 12:29.412
We need to go.

12:29.549 --> 12:31.157
The rain will give over soon.

12:31.292 --> 12:34.323
Your father will be very angry
if we're late. Please.

12:34.459 --> 12:38.522
Stop worrying. It will
give over. I promise it will.

12:38.659 --> 12:40.996
Yeah, but the sky
is black, Cathy.

12:41.131 --> 12:43.970
No, no, no, no. You see there?

12:47.870 --> 12:49.140
Blue.

12:50.539 --> 12:52.277
But that's not enough blue
to get us back.

12:52.413 --> 12:56.476
It is. You'll see. For blue
is blue, no matter how small.

13:14.562 --> 13:16.161
Where have you been?

13:18.465 --> 13:20.805
I said, where have you been?

13:20.942 --> 13:22.201
We were caught
in a storm, Papa.

13:22.338 --> 13:24.742
It is my birthday, Catherine,

13:24.879 --> 13:26.407
and you have kept me waiting.

13:27.840 --> 13:29.644
I believe you do not care
for me at all.

13:29.780 --> 13:32.582
Of course I do, Papa. You're
the best father in the world.

13:32.719 --> 13:34.379
I am so sorry.

13:34.514 --> 13:36.186
You shall be sorry

13:36.323 --> 13:39.386
when it's your own birthday
and I forget it.

13:39.523 --> 13:41.819
Let's have supper
and celebrate properly.

13:44.092 --> 13:45.130
It's cold.

13:45.765 --> 13:46.758
Papa.

13:54.635 --> 13:57.242
It's my fault, sir.

13:57.378 --> 13:59.171
Not Cathy's. She wanted to
turn back but I ignored her.

13:59.306 --> 14:01.005
Heathcliff, please.

14:01.140 --> 14:02.748
All she has spoken of all day
is you and your birthday.

14:04.719 --> 14:06.416
-Is this true?
-No.

14:06.552 --> 14:09.522
I swear it. She's not
to blame.

14:09.656 --> 14:11.423
Are you trembling?

14:11.558 --> 14:14.720
Stop at once. You make me feel
like a brute. Stop it, I say.

14:14.855 --> 14:16.091
Papa, please.
It was not his fault.

14:16.225 --> 14:19.867
I feed you, and clothe you,

14:20.003 --> 14:23.204
and save you
from poverty and despair.

14:23.338 --> 14:29.238
I am the kindest man alive,
and you dare to tremble at me.

14:29.375 --> 14:31.108
I'll give you something
to tremble about!

14:31.245 --> 14:33.805
-Take her, Nelly! Take her!
-Papa, no! No!

14:33.941 --> 14:36.544
-No, no! Get off me! No! No!
-Come here, you dog!

14:37.144 --> 14:38.576
Go!

14:38.712 --> 14:40.754
- Heathcliff! No!
- Come here!

14:40.888 --> 14:43.220
No! No, no, no!

14:43.356 --> 14:44.924
Hold still!

14:45.059 --> 14:47.086
Hold still, you dog!

14:47.223 --> 14:49.425
No! Heathcliff.

14:49.561 --> 14:53.032
You dog. Bark!

15:11.543 --> 15:13.320
Heathcliff.

15:13.455 --> 15:16.385
Heathcliff.

15:18.757 --> 15:19.785
What's he done?

15:21.256 --> 15:22.519
Oh, you're bleeding.

15:22.654 --> 15:24.658
Heathcliff, why did you lie?

15:24.792 --> 15:27.132
It was my fault we were late.
Not yours.

15:29.727 --> 15:31.730
I couldn't see him hurt you.

15:34.032 --> 15:37.105
But this hurts me.
Don't you understand?

15:37.240 --> 15:39.772
Heathcliff, this hurts me.

15:39.907 --> 15:44.017
I will take this and more...

15:45.521 --> 15:46.548
every day...

15:47.985 --> 15:49.083
if it spares you.

15:55.928 --> 15:57.030
Heathcliff...

15:59.665 --> 16:00.726
Yes?

16:02.570 --> 16:03.597
I'm sorry.

16:04.430 --> 16:05.938
Don't be sorry.

16:06.074 --> 16:09.141
Don't ever be sorry
for me, Cathy.

16:10.277 --> 16:12.672
For I would do it
again and again.

16:17.014 --> 16:18.315
Then we're doomed.

16:23.021 --> 16:24.189
What can I do?

16:26.829 --> 16:29.129
Nothing.

16:31.491 --> 16:33.198
Just stay with me.

17:25.788 --> 17:26.878
Heathcliff.

17:29.119 --> 17:30.156
Heathcliff.

17:33.686 --> 17:35.294
Answer me, you brute.

17:37.094 --> 17:38.060
Are you awake?

17:38.197 --> 17:40.562
No.

17:42.904 --> 17:44.828
-Now?
-Catherine!

17:44.964 --> 17:46.773
I was up all night
with the horse.

17:46.909 --> 17:48.640
What could be so important?

17:48.774 --> 17:52.937
Thrushcross Grange is sold.
We have neighbors.

17:57.885 --> 17:59.352
They are called Linton.

17:59.486 --> 18:02.120
- A family?
- A bachelor and his ward.

18:02.257 --> 18:04.284
He made his fortune
in textiles.

18:05.420 --> 18:07.292
God. Look at it all.

18:09.524 --> 18:11.759
He must be very rich indeed.

18:13.829 --> 18:16.092
I suppose he shall
fall in love with me.

18:19.242 --> 18:20.606
I suppose he shall
fall in love with--

18:20.742 --> 18:21.769
I heard you.

18:26.475 --> 18:28.148
It would be nice to be rich.

18:29.778 --> 18:31.281
What should you do,
Heathcliff?

18:31.415 --> 18:33.220
-What?
-If you were rich.

18:33.354 --> 18:36.355
I suppose I'd do
what all rich men do. I'd...

18:38.288 --> 18:39.522
live in a big house.

18:41.062 --> 18:42.789
And be cruel to my servants.

18:44.699 --> 18:45.826
Take a wife.

18:47.836 --> 18:49.564
A wife? What wife?

18:49.700 --> 18:53.833
I... I've always
looked fondly on...

18:56.735 --> 18:58.403
Rose from The Crown.

18:58.540 --> 19:00.181
The landlord's daughter.

19:01.648 --> 19:03.978
She's quite the plainest girl
I ever laid eyes on.

19:04.115 --> 19:07.816
And dull too. Shockingly dull.
She's practically a simpleton.

19:09.755 --> 19:11.887
I cannot sit here all day
talking nonsense with you.

19:12.021 --> 19:14.525
After all, the Lintons may
call on me at any moment.

19:16.794 --> 19:19.723
I warn you,
if they do not come soon,

19:19.857 --> 19:21.696
I shall feel snubbed.

19:21.831 --> 19:23.396
And you will have
a quarrel with them

19:23.532 --> 19:25.567
before you have even met.

19:25.702 --> 19:27.538
That would be a feat
even for you.

19:29.408 --> 19:31.569
We are
a very important family.

19:31.706 --> 19:32.905
Perhaps they do not know.

19:34.679 --> 19:36.806
Earnshaws have been here
since 1500.

19:36.943 --> 19:38.713
It is written above our door!

19:39.550 --> 19:41.347
Why do they not come?

19:41.484 --> 19:42.881
It has only been a week.

19:43.016 --> 19:44.857
In fact, we're likely
far superior

19:44.992 --> 19:46.425
to Mr. Linton's family,

19:46.560 --> 19:48.352
who after all
made their fortune in velvet.

19:48.486 --> 19:51.628
It is not at all the same
thing as land. Not at all.

19:51.762 --> 19:53.730
Perhaps they're waiting
for me to call on them.

19:53.867 --> 19:55.028
No.

19:55.165 --> 19:56.599
Why not?

19:56.734 --> 19:59.095
Because a lady cannot go
to a house unannounced.

19:59.230 --> 20:00.898
It is not done.
They would be shocked.

20:01.035 --> 20:04.034
They would not.
They would be delighted.

20:04.169 --> 20:05.571
As are all who have
the pleasure

20:05.706 --> 20:06.741
of making my acquaintance.

20:08.349 --> 20:10.283
Perhaps that is
why they have not come.

20:11.485 --> 20:14.512
They may be intimidated,
poor things.

20:14.649 --> 20:15.886
Yes, I'm sure that's it.

20:17.125 --> 20:18.253
Work on your tapestry.

20:18.389 --> 20:19.758
I hate my tapestry.

20:21.527 --> 20:23.424
I was not bored
before they came.

20:23.561 --> 20:25.398
Now I'm so bored I might die.

20:25.533 --> 20:28.094
What're you-- Heathcliff!
How dare you!

20:28.228 --> 20:31.263
I have had enough
of hearing about Mr. Linton.

20:31.398 --> 20:35.132
Heathcliff, I... I cannot
get down in these skirts.

20:35.268 --> 20:36.738
Well, then you'll have to
take 'em off.

20:38.872 --> 20:41.246
You will be so very sorry

20:41.383 --> 20:43.944
when I fall out of this tree
and die!

20:45.248 --> 20:46.287
Help!

21:47.414 --> 21:48.844
Are you pleased with yourself?

21:55.152 --> 21:56.551
Very.

21:59.119 --> 22:01.018
Get off! It was just
a loose pebble.

22:01.155 --> 22:02.987
Give me my hat, woman.
Arsehole.

22:03.124 --> 22:04.529
Careful, sir.

22:04.664 --> 22:05.992
Let's get you
on that horse, sir. Come on.

22:06.128 --> 22:07.995
That's it. Steady.

22:08.129 --> 22:09.496
Get off me.
I know how to ride a horse.

22:09.633 --> 22:10.830
Fuck off, you silly woman.

22:10.967 --> 22:11.771
Careful as you go,
Mr. Earnshaw.

22:11.907 --> 22:12.905
Oh, Heathcliff.

22:13.040 --> 22:14.405
Oh.

22:14.542 --> 22:17.169
I-I fear we had
a run-in the other day.

22:17.979 --> 22:19.675
What did I do?

22:19.809 --> 22:21.877
Oh, don't tell me.
I can't bear it.

22:22.014 --> 22:26.012
Ah, what a wretch I am.
Can you forgive poor Earnshaw?

22:27.988 --> 22:29.212
Yes, sir.

22:29.347 --> 22:31.985
Oh, splendid.
Splendid, boy. Yes.

22:32.121 --> 22:33.994
I knew it couldn't be
as bad as I'd imagined.

22:34.128 --> 22:35.527
Well, I'm off to town

22:35.663 --> 22:37.388
to see if I can't find
that wretched solicitor.

22:37.524 --> 22:39.393
For I know it's he who has
been spending all my money.

22:44.800 --> 22:47.267
What happened the other day?

22:47.404 --> 22:50.943
Nothing much. He just gave me
a cuff around the ear, is all.

22:51.077 --> 22:53.372
Silly old fool.

22:53.508 --> 22:56.042
He must know you could knock
his eyes out if you cared to.

22:56.910 --> 22:58.149
He knows I don't care to.

22:58.284 --> 22:59.584
Well, I wish you would.

23:00.316 --> 23:01.345
Do you?

23:02.983 --> 23:04.523
My only restraint is you.

23:08.563 --> 23:10.320
Then you must be better
for both of us.

23:22.808 --> 23:25.171
- Are you cold, Cath?
- Yes.

23:26.412 --> 23:28.010
Let me make you a fire.

23:28.145 --> 23:30.445
No. Papa will whip you
if you do.

23:30.581 --> 23:31.947
We cannot spare the wood.

23:32.081 --> 23:34.917
Hmm. He can always spare
the wood when he's cold.

23:37.919 --> 23:39.185
He'll not need it tonight.

23:40.319 --> 23:41.621
For his face
has made acquaintance

23:41.757 --> 23:42.688
with the parlor floor.

23:42.822 --> 23:44.863
-Again.
-Hmm.

23:44.999 --> 23:47.797
It did not go well with the
solicitor.

23:49.066 --> 23:53.430
We are ruined, Heathcliff.
There is nothing left.

23:54.771 --> 23:56.334
He's gambled it all away.

24:00.746 --> 24:02.146
I suppose I shall have
to throw myself

24:02.283 --> 24:03.742
at Mr. Linton after all.

24:07.251 --> 24:10.490
Hopefully I'll die of cold
and be spared the shame of it.

24:31.335 --> 24:33.107
Heathcliff!

24:43.648 --> 24:46.724
Do not throw yourself
at Mr. Linton, Cath.

26:34.501 --> 26:35.959
Harder.

26:36.093 --> 26:37.132
Yeah, yeah.

26:38.131 --> 26:40.000
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

26:40.137 --> 26:43.234
Must you do that here, Joseph?

26:43.371 --> 26:44.943
The drain in the yard
is at overflow.

26:45.079 --> 26:47.639
So my skirts
will be nothing but pig scab.

27:05.631 --> 27:06.996
Every moment that passes,

27:07.132 --> 27:09.301
we slide further and further
beyond the pale.

27:09.437 --> 27:10.498
Sorry, Miss Catherine.

27:33.289 --> 27:36.090
"Two households,
both alike in dignity

27:36.225 --> 27:38.589
In fair Verona,
where we lay our scene."

27:38.725 --> 27:41.326
And thus begins the greatest,
most romantic play

27:41.460 --> 27:43.532
I have ever read
in my entire life.

27:43.667 --> 27:47.207
And that is including Othello ,
which you know I loved, Edgar.

27:47.341 --> 27:48.742
I actually believe

27:48.877 --> 27:50.203
that the nurse is the villain
of the story

27:50.339 --> 27:51.678
because she allows
this chaos to ensue,

27:51.813 --> 27:53.207
knowing that they're going
to be doomed

27:53.343 --> 27:54.780
and that there's going to be
so much death.

27:54.916 --> 27:56.816
But I don't really like
the nurse actually.

27:56.952 --> 28:00.879
But anyway, Mercutio
gets killed in the street.

28:01.013 --> 28:02.313
Mercutio.

28:02.450 --> 28:03.886
And Romeo then kills Tybalt

28:04.023 --> 28:05.517
for revenge
for Mercutio's death.

28:05.653 --> 28:08.419
He's murdered in the street.
And everyone sees.

28:08.554 --> 28:11.353
So, Romeo,
he's banished from Verona.

28:11.489 --> 28:12.929
And Juliet gets word of this,

28:13.064 --> 28:16.068
and she's
absolutely devastated.

28:16.204 --> 28:18.762
So she hatches this plan
with Friar Laurence, you see,

28:18.896 --> 28:21.304
and-and she's going to take
this sleeping drink,

28:21.438 --> 28:24.803
and she's going to elope
and no-one's going to know.

28:24.939 --> 28:26.106
And word of this

28:26.242 --> 28:28.507
was supposed to be sent
to Romeo,

28:28.641 --> 28:30.607
so that's where
you-you think it's gonna go.

28:30.743 --> 28:33.676
But someone tells Romeo
that Juliet's dead.

28:33.811 --> 28:35.488
But you see,
Juliet is not dead at all.

28:35.624 --> 28:36.652
-She's only taken...
-No.

28:36.787 --> 28:38.286
...a sleeping draft,

28:38.420 --> 28:41.121
but Romeo did not know,
for he was in Mantua,

28:41.258 --> 28:43.764
and the letters
had not reached him.

28:46.327 --> 28:48.895
What a thorough précis,
Isabella.

28:49.032 --> 28:50.401
I feel quite transported.

28:50.535 --> 28:52.100
Oh, how I cried.

28:52.236 --> 28:53.906
Edgar, I thought
my head might fall off.

28:54.040 --> 28:55.440
Oh, dear.
That would not do.

28:55.576 --> 28:57.272
Well, no, indeed not.

28:57.408 --> 28:59.443
For then I should have nowhere
to put my ribbons.

29:04.011 --> 29:05.578
Edgar!

29:05.713 --> 29:07.178
-What on earth is it? What--
-Edgar, I saw a ghost.

29:07.313 --> 29:08.678
Edgar, I saw a ghost.

29:08.814 --> 29:11.956
I saw a ghost there.
There. By the wall.

29:12.093 --> 29:14.592
Oh, Edgar, it had
the most fearsome visage.

29:14.729 --> 29:16.758
Ghastly pale. It was hideous.

29:16.893 --> 29:18.889
It had dead, evil eyes.

29:19.025 --> 29:22.327
There will be some reasonable
explanation. Let me look.

29:22.464 --> 29:23.868
Edgar, please don't leave me.
Please.

29:24.003 --> 29:26.472
You are quite safe,
I assure you.

29:45.888 --> 29:47.189
May I assist you?

29:48.558 --> 29:51.429
"Have sprained
my ankle on a hideous wall.

29:51.566 --> 29:53.127
Linton has taken me in."

29:53.261 --> 29:54.623
Linton!

29:54.760 --> 29:56.165
"Had cream cake for tea
and chocolate."

29:56.300 --> 29:57.627
Chocolate?

29:57.763 --> 29:59.796
She has underlined chocolate.

29:59.933 --> 30:03.873
Clever little cat.
She'll be in clover.

30:04.008 --> 30:06.369
But she's sprained her ankle.

30:06.505 --> 30:08.013
I will go. I can carry her.

30:08.149 --> 30:09.140
- 'Tis five miles.
- It's nothing.

30:09.275 --> 30:10.541
No, no, no, no, no.

30:10.677 --> 30:12.507
You can't go up there,
you silly boy.

30:12.644 --> 30:14.921
You're a servant, Heathcliff.

30:15.055 --> 30:18.485
This is her chance.
And likely her only one.

30:18.619 --> 30:20.892
Well, she's already
well past spinsterhood.

30:21.028 --> 30:23.727
We can't have you
blundering up there.

30:23.862 --> 30:25.697
Would ruin her prospects.

30:25.832 --> 30:28.758
Do... Nelly, we can't just...

30:32.632 --> 30:34.532
A most impressive fellow,
you know.

30:34.667 --> 30:36.406
A gentleman
through and through.

30:36.541 --> 30:40.007
I mean, he's not quite out of
the top drawer, you know.

30:40.141 --> 30:41.540
Obviously.

30:41.676 --> 30:43.577
But we can overlook
such things, can't we?

30:43.711 --> 30:46.243
As we have done with you,
my dear.

30:46.378 --> 30:47.744
Oh, and the Grange.

30:47.879 --> 30:49.515
You've never seen
anything like it.

30:49.649 --> 30:52.181
The drawing room
is made of crystal.

30:52.318 --> 30:53.517
How is Cathy?

30:53.654 --> 30:55.259
Purring like a kitten.

30:55.393 --> 30:58.387
Waited on hand and foot
by both Linton and his ward.

30:58.523 --> 30:59.865
And what is she like?

31:00.000 --> 31:01.362
- Miss Isabella?
- Yes.

31:01.498 --> 31:04.533
Oh, she's very fine.
Very pretty indeed.

31:04.668 --> 31:05.937
Good.

31:06.073 --> 31:07.100
It is a wonder that Linton

31:07.235 --> 31:08.197
didn't marry her himself.

31:08.333 --> 31:10.000
But still,

31:10.135 --> 31:12.573
I suppose they're more like
brother and sister really.

31:12.708 --> 31:14.872
- When will Cathy be back?
- Soon enough.

31:15.006 --> 31:17.280
She kept that ankle clamped
to a velvet pillow

31:17.416 --> 31:20.351
for as long as is
remotely credible.

31:20.486 --> 31:24.615
Mind you, if Linton is even
half as smitten as he looks,

31:24.750 --> 31:26.750
I doubt
if she'll be back here long.

31:56.413 --> 31:57.848
Whoa!

32:05.224 --> 32:06.296
Oh.

32:19.942 --> 32:21.311
Oh.

32:22.716 --> 32:24.112
Ooh, my poor boots.

32:29.249 --> 32:30.512
Thank you, Joseph.

32:30.649 --> 32:32.857
-Cathy.
-Miss Earnshaw.

32:32.993 --> 32:34.555
What is it?

32:35.895 --> 32:37.794
You are transformed.

32:37.929 --> 32:39.689
It is all Isabella.

32:39.826 --> 32:42.597
She is
the sweetest person alive.

32:42.733 --> 32:45.228
She fixed my hair herself.
It is her special talent.

32:46.933 --> 32:50.303
You know, she has a room
entirely for ribbons.

32:50.438 --> 32:53.805
Just ribbons.

32:55.475 --> 32:56.510
Where is Heathcliff?

33:03.615 --> 33:04.882
Well, here you are.

33:08.795 --> 33:10.194
You're back then.

33:10.861 --> 33:11.888
Oh, is that it?

33:14.000 --> 33:16.002
I've been gone six weeks.

33:16.137 --> 33:18.597
You do not bother yourself
to greet me?

33:18.732 --> 33:21.040
In fact,
I do believe you are hiding.

33:24.272 --> 33:26.342
Oh, how cross you look.

33:26.476 --> 33:29.248
And dirty.
I can smell you from here.

33:29.382 --> 33:31.876
No one could be in any danger
of smelling you.

33:33.144 --> 33:35.049
Just enough perfume
to make the eyes water.

33:35.186 --> 33:37.051
It is lily of the valley.

33:37.186 --> 33:38.519
It is no such thing.

33:41.118 --> 33:42.986
You're angry because
I was gone for so long.

33:45.997 --> 33:47.625
It could not be helped.

33:47.762 --> 33:49.962
I'm not angry, Cathy.
I'm busy.

33:50.099 --> 33:54.263
All right? You came to see me,
lo, here we are, so you have.

33:54.399 --> 33:56.372
Why don't you go and bother
one of the other servants?

33:57.845 --> 33:59.075
Heathcliff, do not--

33:59.211 --> 34:00.839
For God's sake,
will you listen?

34:01.740 --> 34:03.638
I tell you, I have work to do.

34:03.775 --> 34:05.050
I cannot endlessly indulge

34:05.184 --> 34:06.877
every last
wretched whim of yours.

34:09.915 --> 34:11.682
We're not children
anymore, Cathy.

34:11.818 --> 34:13.522
Surely you understand
that now?

34:15.928 --> 34:17.163
I cannot play with you.

34:20.366 --> 34:22.431
As though I could crave
your company

34:23.700 --> 34:26.798
after so many weeks
with Edgar and Isabella.

34:31.878 --> 34:32.903
Carry on with your work.

35:28.260 --> 35:30.794
- Heathcliff, I want--
- You get in there.

35:30.931 --> 35:34.570
Do you hear me?
Come on. Get in there.

35:34.704 --> 35:37.033
Go.

35:50.158 --> 35:52.190
You've been a bad girl.

35:52.325 --> 35:53.984
A very bad girl.

35:54.120 --> 35:56.152
You're not gonna be laughing
in a minute.

36:06.067 --> 36:08.804
Where do you think you're
going, hey? Get back here.

36:08.938 --> 36:11.371
You don't wanna stay here
with me? Stay with Joseph?

36:11.506 --> 36:13.642
Hmm?

36:29.259 --> 36:30.296
What do you want?

36:40.007 --> 36:41.565
This'n, or...

36:45.813 --> 36:47.104
Hmm?

37:00.058 --> 37:01.392
Oh, yeah.

37:05.058 --> 37:08.400
Ooh, fucking hell.

37:11.702 --> 37:13.431
-Pull it harder, Joseph.
-I'll break your teeth.

37:13.568 --> 37:14.973
Pull it harder.

37:15.110 --> 37:17.068
Shh.

37:28.750 --> 37:32.015
Oh, good girl.
Good girl.

37:57.644 --> 37:58.680
You're amazin'.

38:29.807 --> 38:30.977
-Cath...
-No.

39:09.181 --> 39:10.780
Are you feeling quite right?

39:10.915 --> 39:13.052
What? Oh, yes. Fine.

39:24.302 --> 39:25.328
I'm going for a walk.

39:27.864 --> 39:29.436
In those skirts?

39:44.188 --> 39:45.216
Cathy!

40:41.239 --> 40:43.043
- Cathy.
- Oh, God.

40:43.179 --> 40:45.649
-Cath. Cath, it's nothing.
-No. Please go away.

40:45.785 --> 40:47.911
-Go away and leave me alone.
-It's nothing.

40:48.048 --> 40:50.149
Oh, God. Oh, God, I will die.

40:50.285 --> 40:52.757
Don't die.
It's not worth dying over.

40:52.894 --> 40:55.924
How dare you laugh at me,
you devil? This is your doing!

40:57.725 --> 40:59.256
How is it my doing?

41:04.701 --> 41:06.063
-Stop talking.
-Cath.

41:06.199 --> 41:07.471
Stop. Do not talk to me
or look at me.

41:07.607 --> 41:09.301
You're going to
make yourself ill.

41:09.437 --> 41:11.367
Do not ever look at me again!
Stop or you will kill me.

41:20.581 --> 41:21.818
Do not.

41:24.154 --> 41:27.650
Do not. Let go of my hand.

41:27.786 --> 41:28.824
Never.

41:49.148 --> 41:50.583
I have you now.

41:51.984 --> 41:54.586
I can follow you like a dog
to the end of the world.

42:16.342 --> 42:17.367
Put me down.

42:20.571 --> 42:22.780
If you care for me at all,
put me down.

42:31.181 --> 42:32.122
Do not follow me.

42:32.259 --> 42:33.525
I beg of you.

42:45.767 --> 42:47.271
Come on, sir.

42:47.407 --> 42:48.899
For God's sake...

42:49.034 --> 42:50.638
Hold me up.

42:50.774 --> 42:52.611
Don't look at me like that!

42:53.211 --> 42:54.608
I'm ill!

42:54.744 --> 42:57.073
We are all ill.

42:57.210 --> 42:59.416
We are all ill because of you!

42:59.553 --> 43:02.320
Ingrate! Slattern!

43:02.457 --> 43:03.553
-Cathy...
-Not now, Nelly.

43:03.688 --> 43:05.389
-Catherine...
-Not now, Nelly!

43:05.524 --> 43:06.822
Whatever it is, it must...

43:06.959 --> 43:10.586
Mr. Linton is in the parlor.

43:13.563 --> 43:14.799
Mr. Linton?

43:19.832 --> 43:20.970
Mr. Linton.

43:21.903 --> 43:23.168
I am not fit to receive you.

43:23.304 --> 43:24.842
Miss Earnshaw,
that could never be true.

43:24.978 --> 43:27.273
Indeed it is. I... I fear
I must excuse myself.

43:27.407 --> 43:30.640
Must be most distressing
to see your father so...

43:30.777 --> 43:31.816
unwell.

43:34.321 --> 43:35.511
You saw him then.

43:42.955 --> 43:44.060
It is too shaming.

43:44.197 --> 43:45.560
No.

43:45.696 --> 43:46.732
It is all too shaming.

43:47.464 --> 43:48.491
No, no.

43:49.831 --> 43:52.070
I'm sorry, Mr. Linton.

43:52.206 --> 43:53.196
I'm very sorry.

43:53.331 --> 43:55.169
Miss Earnshaw, please, sit.

43:56.400 --> 43:57.940
There is something I must say.

43:59.310 --> 44:00.339
Please.

44:03.282 --> 44:04.310
Please.

44:11.689 --> 44:13.053
If I were in heaven, Nelly,

44:13.189 --> 44:15.923
I should be
extremely miserable.

44:16.060 --> 44:17.861
Because you're not fit
to go there.

44:20.664 --> 44:21.700
Not just that.

44:24.067 --> 44:26.331
It is because
I should be homesick.

44:27.974 --> 44:30.500
Did something pass
between you and Mr. Linton?

44:32.678 --> 44:34.545
He asked me to marry him.

44:34.679 --> 44:36.507
And what was your response?

44:37.482 --> 44:38.717
I accepted him.

44:40.987 --> 44:43.683
Well, be quick, Nelly.
Tell me, was I wrong?

44:43.817 --> 44:45.351
Do you love him?

44:46.484 --> 44:48.625
One could not help
but love Edgar.

44:48.759 --> 44:50.257
Then where is the obstacle?

44:50.824 --> 44:51.896
Here.

44:54.394 --> 44:55.730
In whichever place
the soul lives,

44:55.865 --> 44:57.201
I'm convinced I am wrong.

44:57.337 --> 44:58.364
Why?

45:00.705 --> 45:03.567
Nelly, you know why.

45:06.004 --> 45:07.042
Heathcliff.

45:12.751 --> 45:13.984
 I love him.

45:17.455 --> 45:20.050
 Not because he's handsome,
 Nelly, but because he's...

45:20.186 --> 45:21.827
 more myself than I am.

45:24.588 --> 45:25.924
Whatever our souls
are made of,

45:26.061 --> 45:27.462
his and mine are the same.

45:29.193 --> 45:31.099
Do not sigh at me.

45:34.435 --> 45:36.776
I know you think
I'm a selfish wretch...

45:39.876 --> 45:41.704
but if I marry Mr. Linton,

45:43.474 --> 45:46.148
I could aid Heathcliff
to rise.

45:46.284 --> 45:48.342
I could place him
out of my father's power.

45:48.479 --> 45:50.121
With your husband's money?

45:50.255 --> 45:52.818
You'll find him not so pliable
as you calculate upon.

45:52.953 --> 45:54.691
Why did I ask you?

45:54.826 --> 45:56.323
What would you know about it?

45:58.757 --> 46:01.063
You've never loved anyone
in your whole life.

46:02.526 --> 46:04.436
No one has ever loved you.

46:29.158 --> 46:30.828
You say you love Edgar Linton.

46:30.963 --> 46:32.788
You have accepted
his proposal.

46:33.423 --> 46:34.931
It is done, Cathy.

46:35.068 --> 46:37.198
I do not know what it is
you want from me.

46:40.231 --> 46:41.301
Reassurance?

46:44.103 --> 46:45.206
Compassion?

46:46.480 --> 46:47.912
Some kindness?

46:50.277 --> 46:52.477
You must know, Nelly, you.

46:53.548 --> 46:56.581
It would degrade me
to marry Heathcliff.

46:58.526 --> 47:00.221
We would be beggars.

47:07.530 --> 47:11.900
So he shall never know
how I love him.

48:22.468 --> 48:23.798
Where are you going?

48:23.933 --> 48:25.402
To the Grange to call it off.

48:25.537 --> 48:27.141
I could not sleep last night.

48:27.278 --> 48:29.271
I should never
have accepted Linton.

48:29.405 --> 48:30.437
Cathy, stop!

48:30.574 --> 48:31.747
-Stop!
-What?

48:31.884 --> 48:33.413
Joseph, tell her.

48:34.281 --> 48:36.647
I'm sorry, Miss Earnshaw.

48:36.783 --> 48:39.155
He made off with the horse.
Last night.

48:50.096 --> 48:51.935
Cathy...

48:52.072 --> 48:54.170
I do not think
he is coming back.

48:56.135 --> 48:57.169
Of course he is.

48:57.305 --> 48:59.103
He is only trying to vex me.

48:59.240 --> 49:00.474
You know what he's like.

49:02.013 --> 49:03.641
He would never
leave me, Nelly.

49:04.274 --> 49:05.313
Never.

49:26.000 --> 49:26.998
Did he come?

49:36.046 --> 49:37.444
We could put it off.

49:39.319 --> 49:41.976
It has been a year. It cannot
be put off any longer.

49:50.155 --> 49:51.194
Tighter.

49:58.171 --> 49:59.763
-Tighter.
-This is tight enough.

49:59.898 --> 50:02.404
-Tighter, Nelly.
-But you will not breathe.

50:06.876 --> 50:08.377
Tighter.

51:35.759 --> 51:37.136
God, how I love you.

52:13.103 --> 52:15.371
Cathy. Hello!

52:18.002 --> 52:20.036
Can I give you
your wedding present now?

52:21.907 --> 52:24.943
Oh, it's... it's quite lovely.

52:25.078 --> 52:26.779
I made it the night
that Edgar proposed,

52:26.915 --> 52:29.352
once I knew that you
would join us here forever.

52:32.149 --> 52:33.984
-Is this?
-Your real hair. Yes.

52:34.119 --> 52:35.684
For I had been collecting it
from the brush

52:35.819 --> 52:37.227
while you stayed with us.

52:37.364 --> 52:39.194
I... I knew I could not use
anything else,

52:39.330 --> 52:41.694
for your hair is so singular.

52:45.537 --> 52:49.408
Well, this... must have taken
a very long time.

52:49.542 --> 52:52.837
Oh, no matter.
For I have nothing to do.

52:59.219 --> 53:05.722
Let us put
Little Catherine here.

53:05.857 --> 53:08.920
Oh, next to me.

53:21.073 --> 53:22.730
How extraordinary.

53:24.344 --> 53:26.511
Wait till you see
your dresses, Cathy.

53:28.074 --> 53:30.948
Oh, Edgar.
How many did you have made?

53:31.084 --> 53:33.045
This was all my dear ward.

53:33.180 --> 53:37.044
Isabella knows everything.
She had all of these ordered.

53:37.181 --> 53:40.918
From France
and Belgium and Italy.

53:41.055 --> 53:43.125
All of the ateliers have been
making things

53:43.259 --> 53:44.758
to your measurements.

53:44.892 --> 53:47.227
I had to sacrifice
my ribbon room for it.

53:47.362 --> 53:48.792
Oh, Isabella, no.

53:48.929 --> 53:51.268
It was no hardship...

53:51.403 --> 53:52.860
knowing how pleased
you would be.

53:52.995 --> 53:55.105
Come. Come, there is more.

53:55.240 --> 53:57.202
Oh, Cathy, wait till you see.

53:59.206 --> 54:01.403
Your bedroom. When they asked
me what color it should be,

54:01.539 --> 54:04.106
I said it should be the most
beautiful color in the world.

54:05.484 --> 54:08.412
The color of my wife's
sweet face.

54:08.546 --> 54:09.816
Here, look.

54:11.388 --> 54:12.757
The freckle from your cheek.

54:48.321 --> 54:49.360
Nelly.

54:51.654 --> 54:52.528
Nelly.

54:53.590 --> 54:54.630
Nelly.

54:55.934 --> 54:56.962
Nelly.

54:58.237 --> 55:00.300
-Nelly!
-Yes, Cathy.

55:00.436 --> 55:01.969
Well, you have been quiet.

55:02.105 --> 55:03.133
Quiet?

55:03.976 --> 55:05.133
Since we came.

55:05.267 --> 55:07.543
It is not like you
to be so silent.

55:08.541 --> 55:09.503
Do you disapprove?

55:09.640 --> 55:10.679
Of what?

55:12.645 --> 55:14.075
I don't know.

55:14.212 --> 55:16.179
Perhaps it is
only contentment.

55:18.685 --> 55:20.358
You have no complaints?

55:20.493 --> 55:23.184
What could there be
to complain about?

55:23.321 --> 55:26.124
That we are too comfortable?
Too warm?

55:26.261 --> 55:29.493
That your necklace is too big?
That the dog is too small?

55:29.627 --> 55:30.726
It is too small.

55:30.862 --> 55:32.568
I'll grant you that.

55:33.665 --> 55:35.000
As for the rest?

55:36.372 --> 55:37.441
This is good.

55:39.873 --> 55:41.545
 It is good, Cathy.

55:44.214 --> 55:45.339
Hmm?

56:19.948 --> 56:21.552
Everything all right, my love?

56:22.680 --> 56:23.718
Catherine.

56:24.980 --> 56:26.216
I'm fine.

56:49.909 --> 56:51.274
Darling, what are you doing?

57:11.827 --> 57:13.301
Gosh.

57:32.221 --> 57:35.259
They said the
colors would be periwinkle.

57:35.395 --> 57:37.419
- Please, Edgar!
- Bella.

57:37.553 --> 57:39.526
But, Edgar, I'm grown up.

57:39.663 --> 57:41.456
I'm 21 and a half.

57:41.593 --> 57:43.298
Your age has
nothing to do with it, Bella.

57:43.432 --> 57:44.799
Please.

57:44.935 --> 57:45.896
You've been asking me
for weeks,

57:46.031 --> 57:47.529
and for weeks I have said no.

57:47.663 --> 57:49.300
Yes, but you
have not said why, Edgar.

57:49.436 --> 57:51.572
- Absolutely not.
- Oh, please, Edgar! Please!

57:51.708 --> 57:52.904
Do not press me, Bella.

57:53.041 --> 57:54.176
A hanging is not
an appropriate place

57:54.312 --> 57:55.811
for a young lady.

57:55.947 --> 57:57.674
You are so old-fashioned.
Tell him, Catherine.

57:57.808 --> 57:59.009
No, he is right.

57:59.145 --> 58:00.349
You would not like it,
Isabella.

58:00.485 --> 58:01.850
Indeed. Thank you, darling.

58:01.984 --> 58:04.512
I've always found them
quite... barbaric.

58:04.646 --> 58:06.887
- Hmm.
- That is a shame.

58:09.089 --> 58:10.651
For I thought you
would have taken

58:10.786 --> 58:12.894
a particular interest
in this hanging, Catherine.

58:13.394 --> 58:15.157
Why?

58:15.291 --> 58:17.260
Because of who
is being hanged.

58:20.533 --> 58:21.572
What?

58:27.346 --> 58:29.174
It is a woman.

58:33.884 --> 58:35.352
Do you think
they will do it in her skirts?

58:35.486 --> 58:36.817
Oh, for God's sake.

58:36.954 --> 58:38.887
It would be quite indecent,

58:39.023 --> 58:41.389
for surely one could only
look up and see--

58:41.526 --> 58:43.252
Isabella, enough.

58:43.387 --> 58:45.753
Look, you have upset
dear Catherine.

58:45.888 --> 58:47.126
No, no.

58:48.763 --> 58:50.434
I only need some air.

59:12.919 --> 59:15.659
Mrs. Linton. Mrs. Linton.

59:15.795 --> 59:18.760
Oh, Joseph.
Oh, it is good to see you.

59:18.895 --> 59:20.995
-Yeah.
-It has been such a long time.

59:22.267 --> 59:23.759
How are you?

59:23.896 --> 59:25.301
How is Zillah?

59:25.437 --> 59:29.036
Zillah? Gone. Married.

59:29.899 --> 59:31.402
Oh.

59:31.536 --> 59:33.276
Yeah, she's got a little...
a little boy now.

59:33.411 --> 59:34.644
Tubby little rascal.

59:34.779 --> 59:37.239
See them
in the village sometimes.

59:37.373 --> 59:39.148
-She doesn't greet me.
-Oh.

59:39.282 --> 59:42.646
But it wouldn't look well, her
talking to someone like me.

59:42.782 --> 59:43.819
I know that.

59:46.284 --> 59:47.423
I'd embarrass her.

59:47.560 --> 59:50.189
No. I don't think that's true.

59:52.291 --> 59:53.587
Have you come
to see your father?

59:54.799 --> 59:56.859
How is he?

01:00:19.624 --> 01:00:21.121
Hello, Daughter.

01:00:24.527 --> 01:00:26.291
-Papa.
-Oh.

01:00:27.466 --> 01:00:29.826
"Papa" is it now?

01:00:29.962 --> 01:00:31.600
What has happened?

01:00:31.735 --> 01:00:32.961
What has happened?

01:00:33.097 --> 01:00:35.968
Uh, Zillah is gone,

01:00:36.104 --> 01:00:38.870
and I've no money
to replace her.

01:00:39.007 --> 01:00:41.680
And so, uh, we sink into ruin.

01:00:43.111 --> 01:00:45.277
Edgar sends money, Papa.
I know he does.

01:00:47.015 --> 01:00:49.087
Have you come here
to scold me?

01:00:49.222 --> 01:00:50.654
Uh, no, I...

01:00:50.790 --> 01:00:52.647
I came to wish you
a happy Christmas.

01:00:53.557 --> 01:00:55.325
And to see how you are.

01:00:55.460 --> 01:00:57.894
And how do you find me?

01:01:01.190 --> 01:01:02.361
Quite well.

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:08.871
Not dead, you mean.

01:01:10.944 --> 01:01:15.880
You do look well, however.
Mmm.

01:01:16.014 --> 01:01:19.113
Gladdens my heart
to see you so happy, Catkin.

01:01:20.414 --> 01:01:23.346
Perhaps you might share
some of that happiness

01:01:23.480 --> 01:01:27.417
with your poor,
lonely, old papa.

01:01:27.554 --> 01:01:30.861
Just give him a little bit
more to get by on.

01:01:32.255 --> 01:01:33.929
You know I cannot, Papa.

01:01:35.966 --> 01:01:37.865
For you will only
gamble it away.

01:01:38.002 --> 01:01:40.568
And what will you
spend it on, eh?

01:01:40.703 --> 01:01:43.204
More garish jewels?

01:01:43.338 --> 01:01:47.077
More tawdry geegaws
to dangle about your person?

01:01:47.211 --> 01:01:50.947
Well, I suppose
I should not begrudge it.

01:01:51.913 --> 01:01:53.874
You've had no children

01:01:54.009 --> 01:01:56.078
and nothing to do except
make yourself ridiculous.

01:01:57.680 --> 01:02:02.618
No children
in all these years.

01:02:02.754 --> 01:02:06.256
That fine husband of yours
not up to it, I suppose.

01:02:06.391 --> 01:02:08.265
-Or perhaps it's you--
-Stop!

01:02:10.600 --> 01:02:11.725
-There!
-No!

01:02:13.268 --> 01:02:16.071
Since you will toss
your coins on the floor,

01:02:16.205 --> 01:02:19.775
you will stay
and watch me grope for them,

01:02:19.911 --> 01:02:22.279
since that is what
you meant by it.

01:02:34.591 --> 01:02:35.618
I'm sorry.

01:02:37.027 --> 01:02:39.390
Catherine. Catherine.

01:02:41.466 --> 01:02:42.666
It's all right.

01:02:42.801 --> 01:02:45.132
It's all right.
It's all right.

01:02:47.370 --> 01:02:51.632
You're a very brave,
very good girl, my darling.

01:02:51.768 --> 01:02:54.942
You have survived
that wretched place.

01:02:55.079 --> 01:02:56.847
You need never
go back there again.

01:02:58.113 --> 01:02:59.950
I do not know why I went back.

01:03:07.452 --> 01:03:09.822
There is nothing for me there.

01:03:12.163 --> 01:03:15.262
Oh, my.

01:03:16.331 --> 01:03:19.030
Oh, look at this.

01:03:19.167 --> 01:03:20.470
Happy Christmas, Nelly, dear.

01:03:20.604 --> 01:03:21.671
Thank you, Cathy.

01:03:21.807 --> 01:03:24.171
Oh.

01:03:27.337 --> 01:03:29.711
Oh.

01:03:29.847 --> 01:03:31.846
A book of friendship.

01:03:31.981 --> 01:03:33.584
Oh. Oh, you drew that?

01:03:33.718 --> 01:03:35.849
Yes. Yes. That is you and I.

01:03:37.279 --> 01:03:40.451
Oh. Ribbons.

01:03:41.927 --> 01:03:43.021
That is
your beautiful silhouette

01:03:43.155 --> 01:03:44.387
that I watched one day

01:03:44.524 --> 01:03:45.863
from your room.

01:03:45.998 --> 01:03:47.559
-Oh, look at this.
-What on Earth is that?

01:03:47.694 --> 01:03:51.727
Yes, this is, um, a rose
which reminded me of you also.

01:03:51.861 --> 01:03:54.166
The most beautiful rose
in the world.

01:03:54.303 --> 01:03:55.665
- Beautiful.
- Oh.

01:03:55.799 --> 01:03:56.869
Remember the day

01:03:57.005 --> 01:03:58.337
that we went walking,

01:03:58.472 --> 01:04:00.272
and you picked out
a mushroom and you said,

01:04:00.407 --> 01:04:02.109
-"What a lovely mushroom"?
-Yes.

01:04:02.245 --> 01:04:04.880
Well, I commemorated it
in decoupage.

01:04:06.809 --> 01:04:08.082
God.

01:04:08.216 --> 01:04:09.380
It's fantastic news,
Catherine.

01:04:09.514 --> 01:04:11.219
All round.
It's fantastic news.

01:04:11.354 --> 01:04:13.858
I have never been happier.

01:04:13.993 --> 01:04:16.085
So you are excited
to become a father then?

01:04:16.220 --> 01:04:17.721
I am giddy.

01:04:17.856 --> 01:04:19.159
I feel like a chit fresh out
of the schoolroom.

01:04:19.293 --> 01:04:21.699
You clever thing.

01:04:24.330 --> 01:04:25.860
Will you stay here tonight?

01:04:27.003 --> 01:04:28.103
Nothing would please me more.

01:04:30.107 --> 01:04:32.206
But you need your rest,
my love.

01:04:32.341 --> 01:04:34.704
And you will not rest
if I stay here with you.

01:04:36.044 --> 01:04:37.714
Good night.

01:04:37.848 --> 01:04:38.983
Good night, my love.

01:04:40.049 --> 01:04:41.776
How wonderful.

01:07:02.594 --> 01:07:03.721
Heathcliff.

01:07:08.897 --> 01:07:09.958
Heathcliff.

01:07:14.939 --> 01:07:16.931
Oh, what a wicked trick!

01:07:33.923 --> 01:07:35.257
I dared not hope.

01:07:40.799 --> 01:07:41.891
Let me look at you.

01:07:47.063 --> 01:07:49.931
Oh, you are handsome.
You brute.

01:07:54.009 --> 01:07:55.542
And rich.

01:07:59.213 --> 01:08:00.481
Does that amuse you?

01:08:04.547 --> 01:08:05.749
Not in the least.

01:08:21.469 --> 01:08:24.603
Come. We must not
get the mopes.

01:08:27.471 --> 01:08:28.508
Come to dinner.

01:08:30.040 --> 01:08:32.149
Everyone will be
so delighted to see you.

01:08:35.019 --> 01:08:37.316
I ruined my dress

01:08:37.452 --> 01:08:39.317
climbing up there
to get to him,

01:08:39.453 --> 01:08:40.883
and he did not move an inch.

01:08:43.862 --> 01:08:45.524
So you have been abroad?

01:08:45.661 --> 01:08:49.530
Oh, Edgar, look at him.
Of course he has.

01:08:49.664 --> 01:08:52.532
Tell us, Heathcliff,
where have you been?

01:08:52.667 --> 01:08:54.969
What have you been doing
these past years?

01:08:55.105 --> 01:08:56.206
Was it very exciting?

01:08:57.105 --> 01:08:58.131
At times.

01:09:02.211 --> 01:09:05.778
Is that all? "At times"?

01:09:05.913 --> 01:09:10.113
After near five years,
it was exciting "at times"?

01:09:10.248 --> 01:09:11.321
Mmm.

01:09:23.359 --> 01:09:25.132
I see you want me
to press it out of you.

01:09:27.001 --> 01:09:29.306
Well, I will not beg you
for your story, Heathcliff.

01:09:30.870 --> 01:09:32.506
In fact,
I am beginning to suspect

01:09:32.641 --> 01:09:34.745
-that it was very boring.
-It wasn't.

01:09:34.881 --> 01:09:36.209
Perhaps he was a pirate.

01:09:36.344 --> 01:09:37.710
Perhaps I was.

01:09:37.844 --> 01:09:40.351
Oh, dear. Surely not.

01:09:40.485 --> 01:09:42.780
I really don't care
what you have been doing.

01:09:44.218 --> 01:09:45.420
Do I, Edgar?

01:09:46.524 --> 01:09:49.722
Darling, have I
even mentioned Heathcliff?

01:09:51.228 --> 01:09:52.955
I do not believe so, my love.

01:09:53.091 --> 01:09:55.624
You see?
Keep your secrets, Heathcliff.

01:09:55.759 --> 01:09:57.090
And we will have to assume

01:09:57.227 --> 01:09:59.599
that your fortune
was most ill-gotten.

01:09:59.734 --> 01:10:01.365
Where are you staying?

01:10:01.501 --> 01:10:03.240
At Wuthering Heights.

01:10:04.504 --> 01:10:06.265
No, you... you mustn't.

01:10:07.202 --> 01:10:09.071
The place is no more
than a ruin.

01:10:10.315 --> 01:10:12.073
Tell him, Edgar.
He must come here.

01:10:13.074 --> 01:10:15.117
-Indeed. If he... If...
-No.

01:10:15.252 --> 01:10:16.914
No, I would rather be home.

01:10:17.049 --> 01:10:19.949
Home? Yes, I suppose it is
a sort of home for you.

01:10:20.085 --> 01:10:22.457
Yes, I should say so,
since I bought it.

01:10:24.092 --> 01:10:25.786
You did not.

01:10:25.923 --> 01:10:27.925
Oh, how wonderful.

01:10:28.993 --> 01:10:31.895
For us to have a neighbor.

01:10:34.070 --> 01:10:35.103
Wonderful.

01:10:52.888 --> 01:10:58.122
He is the most handsome man
I ever saw.

01:10:58.257 --> 01:10:59.296
Who is?

01:11:00.759 --> 01:11:03.761
Mr. Heathcliff, of course.

01:11:03.896 --> 01:11:06.132
Heathcliff?
He would devour you.

01:11:06.268 --> 01:11:08.668
Oh! He would not.

01:11:09.632 --> 01:11:11.232
He would indeed.

01:11:12.401 --> 01:11:15.576
He is rough and wild
and of wicked temper.

01:11:15.712 --> 01:11:17.842
Why would you say such things?

01:11:18.477 --> 01:11:19.743
He is your friend.

01:11:19.878 --> 01:11:21.416
Yes, it is because
he is my friend

01:11:21.553 --> 01:11:24.252
that I can say it
with such certainty.

01:11:24.386 --> 01:11:26.323
Oh, you are funny, Isabella.

01:11:28.218 --> 01:11:31.021
He would crush you
like a sparrow's egg.

01:11:33.289 --> 01:11:35.333
You are a dog
in the manger, Cathy!

01:11:43.970 --> 01:11:46.069
Do you think I speak
from jealousy?

01:11:47.304 --> 01:11:49.837
I only meant
to save you from humiliation.

01:11:49.973 --> 01:11:51.547
By all means, pursue him.

01:11:53.014 --> 01:11:55.649
I'm sure he'll find
your efforts greatly amusing.

01:11:59.617 --> 01:12:00.551
As will I.

01:12:32.854 --> 01:12:35.215
 Oh, it will be some game.

01:12:35.350 --> 01:12:37.525
For you two
have never quarreled.

01:12:37.661 --> 01:12:39.358
What could there be
to quarrel about?

01:12:39.493 --> 01:12:40.859
I'll be back by supper.

01:12:48.570 --> 01:12:49.637
Goodbye, darling.

01:12:52.936 --> 01:12:54.477
-Thank you.
-Sir.

01:13:05.022 --> 01:13:08.316
I'm sure you know why Isabella
has savaged my poor doll.

01:13:11.519 --> 01:13:13.825
It is because she is
quite besotted with you.

01:13:13.960 --> 01:13:16.764
Hmm.
Indeed, I had not noticed.

01:13:17.694 --> 01:13:19.395
You know she is.

01:13:19.530 --> 01:13:22.063
But now that you bring it to
my attention, she is pretty.

01:13:22.197 --> 01:13:24.607
-Heathcliff...
-And rich.

01:13:24.741 --> 01:13:26.266
She's not been shy
about the inheritance

01:13:26.401 --> 01:13:28.204
settled upon her
once she marries.

01:13:29.875 --> 01:13:32.450
And she likes me, you say?

01:13:34.417 --> 01:13:36.279
Why don't we ask her?

01:13:36.414 --> 01:13:38.647
For I am quite certain
she's hovering by the door,

01:13:38.781 --> 01:13:40.116
listening to us.

01:13:41.124 --> 01:13:42.152
Isabella?

01:13:43.392 --> 01:13:45.494
Isabella, come in, dear.

01:13:45.629 --> 01:13:47.663
We know you are there.

01:13:50.995 --> 01:13:52.469
Shall I come and fetch you?

01:13:59.739 --> 01:14:01.944
Oh, look, Heathcliff.

01:14:02.081 --> 01:14:03.646
Oh!

01:14:03.780 --> 01:14:06.472
Someone who admires you
even more than I do.

01:14:09.313 --> 01:14:12.223
Poor thing is breaking
her heart over you.

01:14:12.357 --> 01:14:14.150
-Cathy, please.
-No! No, no, no.

01:14:14.285 --> 01:14:15.551
-Excuse me.
-Don't run away, dearest.

01:14:15.687 --> 01:14:17.453
Don't run away.

01:14:17.588 --> 01:14:20.927
You see, Isabella thinks that
if only I would step aside,

01:14:21.061 --> 01:14:23.432
she would shoot a shaft
of light into your soul

01:14:23.569 --> 01:14:25.024
that would make you
a gentleman.

01:14:25.161 --> 01:14:27.365
No!

01:14:27.501 --> 01:14:29.639
Do not run.

01:14:29.775 --> 01:14:32.498
I will not be named
a dog in the manger again.

01:14:32.634 --> 01:14:35.435
I will go. You stay.

01:14:37.249 --> 01:14:38.807
Have him to yourself.

01:14:38.942 --> 01:14:40.341
Show him your dolls.

01:14:42.251 --> 01:14:43.278
No.

01:14:48.084 --> 01:14:50.990
You are a dog in the manger.

01:14:51.125 --> 01:14:53.157
You have no interest in her.
You know you do not.

01:14:53.758 --> 01:14:54.894
Leave her alone.

01:14:55.859 --> 01:14:58.163
Why should I?

01:14:58.300 --> 01:15:01.063
If it's kissing she wants,
I'm more than happy to oblige.

01:15:01.199 --> 01:15:02.937
-You will not.
-I have a right to

01:15:03.071 --> 01:15:06.409
if she chooses, and you have
no right to object.

01:15:06.546 --> 01:15:08.777
I'm not your husband,
remember?

01:15:10.375 --> 01:15:12.372
You have no right
to be jealous of me.

01:15:12.507 --> 01:15:14.409
Do not scratch
at me, Heathcliff.

01:15:14.544 --> 01:15:16.582
I have been nothing but kind
since your return.

01:15:16.717 --> 01:15:19.017
No?

01:15:20.551 --> 01:15:23.187
Have I chastised you once
for your desertion?

01:15:24.891 --> 01:15:27.155
Have I delivered
a single rebuke?

01:15:27.292 --> 01:15:28.565
These past years,
I have not known

01:15:28.700 --> 01:15:30.365
if you were alive or dead.

01:15:30.500 --> 01:15:33.102
And you dare to upbraid me?

01:15:33.239 --> 01:15:34.398
When the fault is yours!

01:15:34.534 --> 01:15:35.602
Mine?

01:15:35.738 --> 01:15:37.168
-How have I wronged you?
-How?

01:15:39.745 --> 01:15:42.338
You knew I loved you,
and you disregarded it.

01:15:44.375 --> 01:15:46.513
Don't say you did not.

01:15:46.648 --> 01:15:48.843
You treated me infernally.

01:15:48.977 --> 01:15:50.015
Do you hear?

01:15:50.749 --> 01:15:52.921
Infernally.

01:15:53.058 --> 01:15:55.257
And if you flatter yourself
that I don't perceive it,

01:15:55.393 --> 01:15:56.958
then you are a fool.

01:15:57.093 --> 01:15:59.789
And if you think a few
sweet words will console me,

01:15:59.925 --> 01:16:02.328
then you are an idiot.

01:16:02.464 --> 01:16:03.664
And if you fancy

01:16:03.801 --> 01:16:06.130
that you can
marry Linton unrevenged,

01:16:06.264 --> 01:16:07.968
I will convince you
of the contrary.

01:16:09.566 --> 01:16:12.575
Oh, there can be no peace
between us, Catherine.

01:16:12.710 --> 01:16:14.742
I was a fool
to think otherwise.

01:16:14.878 --> 01:16:17.009
For peace with you
is worse than war.

01:16:18.909 --> 01:16:20.274
So, thank you

01:16:20.410 --> 01:16:22.409
for telling me
Miss Isabella's secret.

01:16:22.543 --> 01:16:24.720
I swear I'll make
the most of it.

01:16:27.287 --> 01:16:29.081
For you are welcome
to torture me to death

01:16:29.218 --> 01:16:30.660
for your own amusement.

01:16:32.790 --> 01:16:36.457
Only please allow me to amuse
myself in the same style.

01:16:41.801 --> 01:16:43.068
Kiss her then.

01:16:45.608 --> 01:16:47.678
Marry her, for all I care.

01:16:49.040 --> 01:16:51.076
It is nothing to me.

01:16:55.115 --> 01:16:56.384
If I thought
you really meant that,

01:16:56.520 --> 01:16:58.050
I'd cut my own throat.

01:16:58.817 --> 01:17:00.283
So cut it.

01:17:01.582 --> 01:17:04.020
Only do not do it
on this carpet.

01:17:04.154 --> 01:17:05.619
For it is Edgar's favorite,

01:17:05.754 --> 01:17:08.390
and he would be very sorry
to see it ruined.

01:17:22.339 --> 01:17:23.377
I do not think
we should receive

01:17:23.514 --> 01:17:25.210
Mr. Heathcliff anymore.

01:17:29.850 --> 01:17:31.315
Whatever you wish, my dear.

01:17:31.450 --> 01:17:33.317
Hmm.

01:17:52.370 --> 01:17:54.739
 Poor little Heathcliff.

01:17:57.505 --> 01:17:59.442
I'm in no mood
for you tonight.

01:17:59.578 --> 01:18:03.018
Oh, I just thought you might
like a little company.

01:18:04.822 --> 01:18:06.181
There is gin
on the side table.

01:18:06.315 --> 01:18:07.687
Let that be your companion.

01:18:07.823 --> 01:18:11.058
Oh? Oh, thank you, dear boy.

01:18:11.192 --> 01:18:13.295
You are good
to your old papa, aren't you?

01:18:15.930 --> 01:18:18.026
It's a grim joke, my boy.

01:18:18.162 --> 01:18:19.736
Is it not?

01:18:22.168 --> 01:18:24.806
My dream in bringing you here

01:18:24.941 --> 01:18:27.272
was to make
a gentleman of you.

01:18:27.407 --> 01:18:31.241
Uh, and now, to look at us...

01:18:31.376 --> 01:18:32.908
...who could tell
which was which?

01:18:33.042 --> 01:18:35.181
Mmm.

01:18:37.085 --> 01:18:40.119
It still is...
It's not enough, is it?

01:18:41.326 --> 01:18:42.619
Not for her.

01:18:45.728 --> 01:18:47.720
You're still just her pet.

01:18:49.197 --> 01:18:52.901
You'll only ever be her pet.

01:19:13.082 --> 01:19:14.120
Joseph?

01:19:23.792 --> 01:19:25.195
Catherine.

01:19:25.332 --> 01:19:27.629
-Is he in there? Is he? Is he?
-Don't.

01:19:47.486 --> 01:19:51.620
I'm sorry, Papa. I'm sorry.

01:20:09.845 --> 01:20:11.078
I'm sorry.

01:20:22.221 --> 01:20:24.224
Cath...

01:20:25.455 --> 01:20:27.226
Please. Please.

01:20:36.365 --> 01:20:37.665
Cathy!

01:20:41.939 --> 01:20:43.176
Cathy!

01:20:46.817 --> 01:20:49.010
-Cath.
-Do not follow me.

01:20:49.144 --> 01:20:50.518
Wait.

01:20:50.652 --> 01:20:51.587
Leave me alone.

01:20:51.722 --> 01:20:53.582
-Cath!
-Leave me alone.

01:20:56.494 --> 01:20:57.520
You're wet.

01:20:58.991 --> 01:21:00.323
I am not.

01:21:00.457 --> 01:21:02.691
-You're cold.
-I am not!

01:21:02.826 --> 01:21:05.097
You will catch your death.
It will be your fault.

01:21:05.233 --> 01:21:07.699
It will be yours!

01:21:12.671 --> 01:21:16.436
No! No! Put me down!

01:21:16.573 --> 01:21:19.239
You must put me down!

01:21:23.279 --> 01:21:24.813
Do not hit me.

01:21:24.947 --> 01:21:26.813
I only mean to keep you dry,
you wretched shrew.

01:21:27.690 --> 01:21:28.955
I hate you.

01:21:29.090 --> 01:21:31.654
What are you doing? Do not...

01:21:53.713 --> 01:21:57.611
I should not have kicked him.
That was bad.

01:21:57.746 --> 01:21:59.081
I can only admire
your restraint

01:21:59.218 --> 01:22:00.914
in limiting it to twice.

01:22:03.218 --> 01:22:07.253
The rain will not last, Cath.
There is some blue yet.

01:22:10.232 --> 01:22:12.133
You and I both know
there is none.

01:22:21.636 --> 01:22:23.046
Why did you leave me?

01:22:24.908 --> 01:22:27.780
I thought it would kill me,
Heathcliff.

01:22:27.916 --> 01:22:28.942
Why did you do it?

01:22:31.249 --> 01:22:32.781
Why did I leave you?

01:22:34.660 --> 01:22:36.422
Why did you despise me?

01:22:38.061 --> 01:22:40.152
Why did you betray
your own heart?

01:22:40.289 --> 01:22:44.529
Oh, I heard you that day,
the day you accepted Edgar.

01:22:47.270 --> 01:22:50.271
You said it would degrade you
to marry me.

01:22:54.435 --> 01:22:57.806
No, I... No.

01:22:59.850 --> 01:23:01.611
No, Heathcliff, I...

01:23:01.748 --> 01:23:03.944
You did not hear all.
You did not hear all.

01:23:07.782 --> 01:23:09.488
I said that I loved you.

01:23:18.162 --> 01:23:19.728
I love you.

01:23:30.409 --> 01:23:33.611
You loved me? You loved me?

01:23:35.350 --> 01:23:37.219
Then what right had you
to leave me?

01:23:38.679 --> 01:23:40.090
Answer me. What right?

01:23:40.225 --> 01:23:42.925
Oh, for the poor fancy
you felt for Linton?

01:23:43.062 --> 01:23:45.226
Because misery,
degradation, death,

01:23:45.362 --> 01:23:47.026
nothing that God or Satan
could inflict

01:23:47.160 --> 01:23:48.159
would have parted us.

01:23:48.296 --> 01:23:50.396
You did it, of your own will.

01:23:52.370 --> 01:23:55.361
I have not broken your heart.
You have broken it.

01:23:57.000 --> 01:23:58.932
And in breaking it,
you've broken mine.

01:24:39.311 --> 01:24:40.875
So kiss me again.

01:24:44.383 --> 01:24:46.452
And let us both be damned.

01:25:13.779 --> 01:25:16.180
"Come unto me,
all ye that labor

01:25:16.315 --> 01:25:17.951
and are heavy laden,

01:25:18.088 --> 01:25:19.453
and I will give you rest.

01:25:21.017 --> 01:25:24.389
Take my yoke upon you,
and learn of me;

01:25:24.525 --> 01:25:27.361
for I am meek
and lowly in heart:

01:25:28.596 --> 01:25:30.893
and ye shall find rest
unto your souls.

01:25:33.503 --> 01:25:37.866
For my yoke is easy
and my burden is light."

01:26:25.053 --> 01:26:26.080
Cathy.

01:26:28.190 --> 01:26:29.949
-Catherine.
-Hmm?

01:26:30.085 --> 01:26:32.053
You will be careful,
won't you?

01:26:34.492 --> 01:26:35.792
Does Heathcliff know?

01:26:37.497 --> 01:26:39.625
I do not know what you mean.

01:26:39.762 --> 01:26:41.469
That you are with child.

01:26:42.168 --> 01:26:43.602
No.

01:27:56.375 --> 01:27:57.908
I love you.

01:28:00.116 --> 01:28:01.241
I love you.

01:28:03.315 --> 01:28:04.584
I love you.

01:28:07.220 --> 01:28:08.325
I love you.

01:28:09.960 --> 01:28:11.251
I love you.

01:28:21.303 --> 01:28:23.639
Quick. Be quick. Quick.

01:28:23.774 --> 01:28:24.802
I know.

01:29:03.205 --> 01:29:05.205
This cannot go on.

01:29:06.114 --> 01:29:07.145
Who says so?

01:29:07.282 --> 01:29:08.649
My conscience.

01:29:09.549 --> 01:29:11.146
Then do not listen.

01:29:12.716 --> 01:29:14.083
You are not married.

01:29:14.217 --> 01:29:15.722
You cannot feel the flames
at your feet.

01:29:15.857 --> 01:29:18.322
Well, at least now
your feet are warm, Cath.

01:29:18.456 --> 01:29:19.527
Do not jest.

01:29:22.063 --> 01:29:23.091
Do not.

01:29:30.272 --> 01:29:32.035
Heathcliff, do not...

01:29:33.207 --> 01:29:34.576
I hate you.

01:29:37.543 --> 01:29:38.606
Well, I love you.

01:29:53.832 --> 01:29:54.958
Go.

01:29:56.160 --> 01:29:58.028
Very well.

01:30:00.498 --> 01:30:01.866
Tomorrow?

01:30:03.668 --> 01:30:05.034
I thought we must stop?

01:30:19.189 --> 01:30:20.419
I have to go.

01:30:20.555 --> 01:30:22.920
- No.
- Yes.

01:30:28.429 --> 01:30:32.424
Cath? Cath, what is it?

01:30:34.162 --> 01:30:37.968
Nothing. Only I am so happy.

01:30:41.071 --> 01:30:43.472
-I love you.
-Don't say it.

01:30:43.608 --> 01:30:44.673
I love you.

01:30:46.182 --> 01:30:47.283
You'll kill me.

01:30:47.417 --> 01:30:49.517
-I love you.
-Don't say it.

01:30:49.652 --> 01:30:52.279
-I love you. I love you.
-Don't say it.

01:30:58.328 --> 01:30:59.759
Why do you stay here?

01:31:02.162 --> 01:31:04.599
It's filthy. Why don't you
stay in my old room?

01:31:04.735 --> 01:31:07.932
Because then I cannot lie here
as I do now.

01:31:11.839 --> 01:31:15.435
And imagine that
we are still children.

01:31:15.571 --> 01:31:18.438
And you're asleep
in your bed across the yard.

01:31:20.515 --> 01:31:22.144
And there is still a chance.

01:31:25.623 --> 01:31:27.524
I wish I had never said it.

01:31:28.689 --> 01:31:31.220
I changed my mind immediately.

01:31:31.354 --> 01:31:33.387
I was going to call it off
the next day.

01:31:35.457 --> 01:31:37.325
If I had known
you were listening...

01:31:38.633 --> 01:31:40.360
I always thought you did.

01:31:41.633 --> 01:31:42.670
How could I?

01:31:44.032 --> 01:31:45.498
Because Nelly saw me.

01:31:56.950 --> 01:31:59.479
You will find
another position, Nelly.

01:32:00.221 --> 01:32:01.721
What?

01:32:01.856 --> 01:32:04.483
You will find
another position.

01:32:05.993 --> 01:32:07.927
-Another position?
-Immediately.

01:32:09.962 --> 01:32:11.666
What is it you suspect me of?

01:32:13.730 --> 01:32:14.933
Treason.

01:32:15.734 --> 01:32:16.771
What treason?

01:32:17.807 --> 01:32:21.209
The night that Heathcliff
disappeared,

01:32:21.345 --> 01:32:23.508
he was listening to us.

01:32:23.643 --> 01:32:27.210
He heard. And you knew.

01:32:28.379 --> 01:32:30.542
And you did not tell me
that he was there.

01:32:32.285 --> 01:32:34.481
You did not give me
the opportunity to rectify

01:32:34.617 --> 01:32:36.923
what would become
the worst mistake of my life.

01:32:38.622 --> 01:32:39.661
Why?

01:32:41.132 --> 01:32:42.456
Why, Nelly?

01:32:45.700 --> 01:32:46.966
Do you know what I think?

01:32:50.771 --> 01:32:53.070
I think you like
to see me cry.

01:32:54.074 --> 01:32:56.503
Not half as much
as you like crying.

01:33:03.414 --> 01:33:05.713
You will tell Edgar
you have found a new place.

01:33:05.849 --> 01:33:06.887
And you will go.

01:33:08.015 --> 01:33:09.087
Where will I go?

01:33:12.725 --> 01:33:14.257
I don't care.

01:34:10.781 --> 01:34:11.886
Catherine.

01:34:20.661 --> 01:34:21.994
Yes, darling?

01:34:22.129 --> 01:34:22.990
I think it is best
that you do not see

01:34:23.125 --> 01:34:25.031
Mr. Heathcliff anymore.

01:34:28.606 --> 01:34:30.398
-But, darling, I...
-Don't.

01:34:34.713 --> 01:34:36.075
You were quite right,
of course,

01:34:36.209 --> 01:34:38.739
to welcome him here
while he found his feet.

01:34:38.875 --> 01:34:41.850
But I think it's best we sever
the connection now, don't you?

01:34:43.554 --> 01:34:45.085
It would be most distressing

01:34:45.220 --> 01:34:46.947
if anyone mistook
your natural good-heartedness

01:34:47.084 --> 01:34:48.681
for something untoward.

01:34:49.857 --> 01:34:51.926
Especially given
your condition.

01:34:55.266 --> 01:34:56.293
Of course.

01:34:57.502 --> 01:34:59.562
You are right, as always.

01:34:59.697 --> 01:35:02.431
Thank you, darling, for saving
me from my own foolishness.

01:35:29.731 --> 01:35:31.031
What are you reading?

01:35:34.002 --> 01:35:37.062
Oh, j-just s-some
silly nonsense.

01:35:59.629 --> 01:36:00.654
What on earth was that?

01:36:10.404 --> 01:36:12.907
The swallows get lost
when the wind changes.

01:36:14.535 --> 01:36:16.602
-Let me see to it.
-Don't.

01:36:16.736 --> 01:36:20.575
Please.
I don't want it to suffer.

01:36:26.385 --> 01:36:27.989
If it will make you
feel better.

01:36:42.302 --> 01:36:45.303
Where are you?
I know you are here.

01:36:47.109 --> 01:36:50.010
Are you mad?
You've broken the window.

01:36:50.677 --> 01:36:52.203
You have to go.

01:36:52.339 --> 01:36:53.572
Where were you?

01:36:53.709 --> 01:36:55.047
Heathcliff,
you do not understand.

01:36:55.181 --> 01:36:57.215
Catherine,
is everything all right?

01:36:57.984 --> 01:36:59.387
Yes, my love.

01:36:59.524 --> 01:37:00.818
Well, come back inside.

01:37:00.953 --> 01:37:02.518
He cannot see us.

01:37:03.520 --> 01:37:05.993
- Are you sure?
- Do not--

01:37:08.291 --> 01:37:10.332
No, no. You mustn't.

01:37:10.466 --> 01:37:11.967
I mustn't?

01:37:12.101 --> 01:37:14.200
Wasn't that your tongue
in my mouth, Cathy?

01:37:15.596 --> 01:37:17.565
I'll set the dogs on you.

01:37:21.706 --> 01:37:24.880
And every bite will be
a pleasure coming from you.

01:37:45.901 --> 01:37:47.030
Enough.

01:37:47.165 --> 01:37:49.064
Come on. Back inside.

01:37:49.199 --> 01:37:50.432
Sorry, darling.

01:37:50.567 --> 01:37:51.901
It's freezing.
You'll catch your death.

01:37:52.036 --> 01:37:53.036
I like the cold.

01:37:53.171 --> 01:37:55.241
Yes, but our son may not.

01:38:38.952 --> 01:38:39.913
Tell me.

01:38:44.890 --> 01:38:45.917
Is it mine?

01:38:50.163 --> 01:38:52.166
It is not.

01:38:55.001 --> 01:38:56.598
How can you be sure?

01:38:58.107 --> 01:39:00.536
I was sure
before your return.

01:39:02.271 --> 01:39:03.309
I'm sorry.

01:39:05.815 --> 01:39:07.214
It is Edgar's child.

01:39:14.450 --> 01:39:16.256
Did you think I would mind?

01:39:21.658 --> 01:39:24.263
Did you think
it would stop me?

01:39:28.997 --> 01:39:32.132
Indeed, I only would have
enjoyed it more.

01:39:32.268 --> 01:39:33.537
You fiend.

01:39:36.072 --> 01:39:38.804
I'm amazed he had it in him.

01:39:38.938 --> 01:39:40.710
I'm amazed
he would dare touch you.

01:39:40.845 --> 01:39:43.446
You would be shocked at
the things Edgar dares to do.

01:39:43.582 --> 01:39:45.219
-Would I?
-It would make you blush.

01:39:45.353 --> 01:39:48.816
Is that right?

01:39:56.663 --> 01:40:00.667
It would make even Joseph
and Zillah blush,

01:40:00.804 --> 01:40:02.334
what he does to me.

01:40:05.075 --> 01:40:06.933
And that is how
you found yourself

01:40:07.069 --> 01:40:08.937
in this squalid condition.

01:40:09.073 --> 01:40:10.501
Yes.

01:40:12.907 --> 01:40:15.715
I'm amazed
it didn't happen sooner.

01:40:15.852 --> 01:40:17.976
He barely lets me sleep.

01:40:23.853 --> 01:40:25.758
He cannot keep
his hands off me.

01:40:28.461 --> 01:40:31.594
-He loves me so much.
-You liar.

01:40:32.362 --> 01:40:34.730
He does. He loves me.

01:40:35.464 --> 01:40:36.666
And you love him.

01:40:37.401 --> 01:40:38.599
More than anything.

01:40:38.734 --> 01:40:40.868
More than anyone.
I love him so.

01:40:41.836 --> 01:40:43.375
I've never loved anyone else.

01:40:45.176 --> 01:40:46.206
You bitch.

01:40:53.619 --> 01:40:55.717
-This is how you love him?
-Yes.

01:40:57.194 --> 01:40:58.754
-This is how you love him?
-Yes.

01:41:00.692 --> 01:41:02.063
-This is how you love him?
-Yes.

01:41:05.102 --> 01:41:08.233
-I'll kill him. Yeah.
-Oh, God, yes.

01:41:08.368 --> 01:41:10.562
-I'll crush his ribs.
-Yes.

01:41:10.697 --> 01:41:12.305
I'll tear his heart out.

01:41:13.601 --> 01:41:15.437
I'll slit his throat.

01:41:15.572 --> 01:41:17.803
I'll drink his fucking blood.

01:41:48.572 --> 01:41:49.669
Would you really kill him?

01:41:54.079 --> 01:41:58.319
I'll go to his room directly,
and I'll break his neck.

01:42:00.989 --> 01:42:02.384
Tell me to do it.

01:42:02.520 --> 01:42:04.153
Make me do it.

01:42:19.940 --> 01:42:20.967
Oh, God.

01:42:27.349 --> 01:42:30.219
I said that you
would degrade me.

01:42:30.354 --> 01:42:32.948
I did not know
that I would degrade myself.

01:42:33.082 --> 01:42:36.487
It's only a little shame,
Cath. It will not last.

01:42:36.622 --> 01:42:39.522
Let me go.
Let me go, Heathcliff.

01:42:39.659 --> 01:42:41.526
Listen to me.
This cannot go on.

01:42:43.263 --> 01:42:44.893
Heathcliff, it is done.

01:42:48.101 --> 01:42:49.633
You don't mean it.

01:42:50.300 --> 01:42:51.569
It is done.

01:42:53.908 --> 01:42:55.166
I love you.

01:42:56.736 --> 01:42:58.108
It doesn't matter.

01:42:58.245 --> 01:43:00.105
I love you.

01:43:01.381 --> 01:43:03.284
I love you.

01:43:03.984 --> 01:43:05.253
It is too late.

01:43:09.420 --> 01:43:10.885
You are too late.

01:43:11.992 --> 01:43:13.019
No.

01:43:14.261 --> 01:43:15.561
I'll never forgive you.

01:44:07.546 --> 01:44:09.141
Do you know how this works?

01:44:14.488 --> 01:44:15.950
Would you like me to show you?

01:44:34.767 --> 01:44:36.235
Cathy was right.

01:44:37.573 --> 01:44:39.480
I am rough

01:44:41.412 --> 01:44:42.647
and cruel

01:44:44.318 --> 01:44:46.486
and cold and unfeeling.

01:44:48.387 --> 01:44:50.326
Do you want me to stop?

01:45:03.666 --> 01:45:05.473
I do not love you.

01:45:07.209 --> 01:45:08.806
I will never love you.

01:45:10.938 --> 01:45:12.809
I will treat you abominably.

01:45:14.645 --> 01:45:16.209
Do you want me to stop?

01:45:33.163 --> 01:45:34.968
I will marry you
with the sole purpose

01:45:35.105 --> 01:45:36.668
of tormenting Catherine.

01:45:38.003 --> 01:45:40.804
I will think of her
every moment I am with you.

01:45:43.377 --> 01:45:44.578
Do you want me to stop?

01:45:53.717 --> 01:45:55.588
Do you want me to stop?

01:46:00.995 --> 01:46:02.524
No.

01:46:15.402 --> 01:46:17.806
Isabella?

01:46:17.940 --> 01:46:19.238
Is everything all right?

01:46:23.251 --> 01:46:25.376
Ugh. Filthy creature.

01:46:39.235 --> 01:46:42.096
Will you stop crying?

01:46:42.232 --> 01:46:45.201
Come on.
I've married you, haven't I?

01:46:45.336 --> 01:46:48.203
All I have to ask you is,
are you of marriageable age?

01:46:48.340 --> 01:46:49.474
Yes.

01:46:49.609 --> 01:46:51.310
-Are you free to marry?
-Yes.

01:46:51.445 --> 01:46:52.775
 She is a fool.

01:46:52.912 --> 01:46:55.110
I can bear much, Catherine.

01:46:55.246 --> 01:46:58.050
But I will not stand for you
weeping over that fiend

01:46:58.186 --> 01:46:59.386
in front of me.

01:46:59.523 --> 01:47:01.949
It is enough.
All right? Enough.

01:47:02.086 --> 01:47:03.021
 Are you free to marry?

01:47:03.156 --> 01:47:04.758
Yes.

01:47:04.893 --> 01:47:06.527
Congratulations. You may
kiss the bride, etcetera.

01:47:09.233 --> 01:47:11.697
 I'm so sorry.

01:47:11.834 --> 01:47:13.693
-I cannot help it.
-You will, for God's sake.

01:47:13.829 --> 01:47:15.294
You will help it.

01:47:15.430 --> 01:47:16.834
Get out of my sight
until you're recovered.

01:47:24.909 --> 01:47:26.482
This is indecent, Cathy.

01:47:27.415 --> 01:47:28.814
Pull yourself together.

01:47:47.226 --> 01:47:49.266
 Dear Nelly,

01:47:49.400 --> 01:47:52.800
 I know that Edgar will not
 accept a letter from me,

01:47:52.936 --> 01:47:54.543
 so I am come to you.

01:47:56.269 --> 01:47:58.007
 I cannot begin to describe

01:47:58.143 --> 01:48:00.515
 the trials
 of this last fortnight.

01:48:02.645 --> 01:48:07.077
 I only wish to ask,
 since you know my husband,

01:48:07.214 --> 01:48:08.589
 what have I married?

01:48:11.822 --> 01:48:14.061
 Is Mr. Heathcliff a man?

01:48:15.696 --> 01:48:19.260
 If so, is he mad?

01:48:20.831 --> 01:48:24.539
 If not, is he a devil?

01:48:29.342 --> 01:48:33.009
 I have no doubt that
 he has me under some spell,

01:48:33.145 --> 01:48:36.849
 which I am incapable
 of breaking.

01:48:37.648 --> 01:48:39.181
Oh, s-sorry, sir.

01:48:39.316 --> 01:48:41.182
Do not worry,
Joseph, you can stay.

01:48:43.953 --> 01:48:45.660
You shall not bother us.

01:48:46.825 --> 01:48:48.190
Is that not so, Isabella?

01:48:51.160 --> 01:48:52.831
 He is monstrous.

01:48:54.963 --> 01:48:56.494
 Diabolical.

01:48:59.176 --> 01:49:00.268
 Possessed.

01:49:04.942 --> 01:49:07.307
 Help me, Nelly.

01:49:24.635 --> 01:49:27.061
How goes your search
for a position?

01:49:27.198 --> 01:49:30.731
It does not.
Edgar has forbidden it.

01:49:30.868 --> 01:49:32.773
Hmm. Has he?

01:49:34.474 --> 01:49:36.304
Once again,

01:49:36.440 --> 01:49:39.471
my despair seems to be
your good fortune, Nelly.

01:49:41.509 --> 01:49:43.310
I hope it soothes you
to blame me.

01:49:56.226 --> 01:49:58.261
I told you
they would not read it.

01:49:58.397 --> 01:50:00.334
Well, the letter
was not shocking enough,

01:50:00.471 --> 01:50:01.933
or Nelly would've shown them.

01:50:02.968 --> 01:50:04.803
I thought
it was quite harrowing.

01:50:04.940 --> 01:50:07.173
It could not have been,
or they would respond.

01:50:11.945 --> 01:50:13.305
Well, if you doubt
my competence,

01:50:13.441 --> 01:50:15.343
then why don't you
write a letter?

01:50:17.617 --> 01:50:21.888
Oh, no... You can't.

01:50:30.959 --> 01:50:32.227
Hmm.

01:50:45.941 --> 01:50:47.276
Write another...

01:50:51.782 --> 01:50:53.216
to Cathy directly.

01:50:59.795 --> 01:51:03.489
And then you
will be nice to me.

01:51:06.361 --> 01:51:11.432
Then I will be
very nice to you.

01:51:31.523 --> 01:51:35.027
It has been too long.
I must see Catherine.

01:51:35.163 --> 01:51:38.758
And how will she respect you
if you relent now?

01:51:38.893 --> 01:51:42.364
Think what permissions you
will grant if you comfort her.

01:51:42.499 --> 01:51:44.497
It would be nothing short
of an endorsement.

01:51:45.474 --> 01:51:46.907
You must not see her.

01:51:48.142 --> 01:51:51.112
Hold fast.
Show her you will not bend.

01:51:51.246 --> 01:51:54.343
It is more important than ever
now Heathcliff has returned.

01:51:57.245 --> 01:52:00.184
Heathcliff has returned?

01:52:00.318 --> 01:52:03.450
Isabella has written.
They are at the Heights.

01:52:03.585 --> 01:52:06.360
She wishes most fervently
to see you.

01:52:08.229 --> 01:52:09.928
Well, she can wish all she
wants, but it is in vain.

01:52:10.064 --> 01:52:11.624
Tell her she can go hang
for all I care,

01:52:11.758 --> 01:52:15.769
and tell my wife
to pull herself together.

01:52:15.906 --> 01:52:17.839
I will have order
in this house again.

01:52:38.655 --> 01:52:40.994
How many more weeks of this
must we all endure?

01:52:43.098 --> 01:52:45.929
It is not good for you.
It is not good for the baby.

01:52:46.065 --> 01:52:48.561
-The baby is gone.
-When?

01:52:50.297 --> 01:52:51.334
Have you bled?

01:52:52.374 --> 01:52:53.338
No.

01:52:55.077 --> 01:52:56.603
If you have not bled,
then the baby is fine.

01:52:57.810 --> 01:52:59.507
If you say so.

01:52:59.641 --> 01:53:02.075
Stop it now, Cathy,

01:53:02.210 --> 01:53:03.476
or you will be in danger

01:53:03.611 --> 01:53:05.512
of losing Edgar's
affection forever.

01:53:05.648 --> 01:53:07.515
Heathcliff is gone.
You must accept it.

01:53:07.651 --> 01:53:09.346
Mrs. Heathcliff's fortune
is in London, and--

01:53:09.481 --> 01:53:11.252
Do not call her that.

01:53:11.386 --> 01:53:14.026
-It is her name.
-It is my name.

01:53:15.993 --> 01:53:19.296
I named him. He is mine.

01:53:42.948 --> 01:53:45.156
Oh, shut up. It's Catherine.

01:53:48.027 --> 01:53:50.228
Oh, Nelly. What do you want?

01:54:01.335 --> 01:54:02.635
What is this?

01:54:02.769 --> 01:54:04.242
It's nothing.
She has been insolent.

01:54:08.843 --> 01:54:11.314
This is monstrous.
Isabella, come at once.

01:54:12.520 --> 01:54:15.516
Isabella, stay.

01:54:19.930 --> 01:54:23.293
Heathcliff,
let the poor thing go.

01:54:25.067 --> 01:54:26.431
Can't you see
she must hate you?

01:54:26.566 --> 01:54:27.901
Aye.

01:54:28.038 --> 01:54:30.932
She says so 100 times a day.

01:54:31.066 --> 01:54:32.567
And yet...

01:54:32.701 --> 01:54:36.273
Isabella, if I leave you alone
for half a day,

01:54:36.410 --> 01:54:40.237
won't you come sighing
and wheedling back to me?

01:54:45.387 --> 01:54:49.520
She's a funny creature, Nelly.
No brutality disgusts her.

01:54:49.655 --> 01:54:53.786
No, I must suppose she has
an innate admiration of it.

01:54:55.664 --> 01:54:57.933
So tell Catherine

01:54:58.067 --> 01:55:01.467
I have finally found
my match in degradation.

01:55:01.602 --> 01:55:02.629
Look.

01:55:10.879 --> 01:55:12.738
I will tell her no such thing.

01:55:14.049 --> 01:55:16.215
I want no part
of whatever this is.

01:55:17.116 --> 01:55:19.250
For God's sake, Heathcliff.

01:55:22.652 --> 01:55:24.685
Isabella,
let me take you home.

01:55:28.720 --> 01:55:30.163
Would you like to come home?

01:55:34.262 --> 01:55:35.860
Nelly, I am home.

01:55:52.219 --> 01:55:54.512
Write to Cathy again.

01:55:54.649 --> 01:55:57.090
She cannot ignore me forever.

01:56:02.957 --> 01:56:05.699
 Have any letters
 come for me, Nelly?

01:56:05.834 --> 01:56:07.166
 None at all.

01:56:13.639 --> 01:56:17.111
 Cathy,
 let us call a truce now.

01:56:18.477 --> 01:56:20.839
 For this silence
 will kill us both.

01:56:27.180 --> 01:56:29.512
 I will wait for you every day

01:56:29.648 --> 01:56:31.256
 and every night.

01:56:36.965 --> 01:56:38.428
 Why do you not respond?

01:56:43.872 --> 01:56:46.436
 I love you. I love you.

01:56:47.710 --> 01:56:49.242
 I love you.

01:57:34.714 --> 01:57:35.980
Cathy!

01:57:41.421 --> 01:57:42.389
Cathy!

01:57:48.937 --> 01:57:49.961
Cathy!

01:58:00.946 --> 01:58:02.039
Cathy!

01:58:17.724 --> 01:58:20.959
Cathy, why did you do it?

01:58:26.206 --> 01:58:27.538
 I am sorry.

01:58:30.571 --> 01:58:31.706
 I am sorry.

01:58:47.257 --> 01:58:49.855
Stop it. Stop it.

01:58:49.992 --> 01:58:52.731
It is enough now.
Enough. Get out of bed.

01:58:52.866 --> 01:58:54.060
I fear I cannot.

01:58:54.197 --> 01:58:55.829
You can.

01:58:55.965 --> 01:58:58.505
You can,
you selfish, wicked creature.

01:58:58.640 --> 01:58:59.668
You can.

01:59:01.807 --> 01:59:03.369
I will not stand for
this grotesque performance

01:59:03.503 --> 01:59:05.344
a moment longer.

01:59:05.479 --> 01:59:09.181
You are revolting.
You are both revolting.

01:59:09.316 --> 01:59:11.876
Get out of bed.

01:59:12.010 --> 01:59:14.313
Get out of bed.
Get out of bed.

01:59:25.091 --> 01:59:29.160
Ah, Nelly has
played traitor again.

01:59:30.798 --> 01:59:32.833
Nelly is my hidden enemy.

01:59:40.679 --> 01:59:43.516
What the devil is it?

01:59:43.652 --> 01:59:46.880
"Theatrics," Nelly? These are
the signs of septicemia.

01:59:47.017 --> 01:59:49.520
She said the baby died
some time ago.

01:59:50.685 --> 01:59:52.552
I thought it was a pretense.

01:59:52.686 --> 01:59:53.888
"A pretense"?

01:59:55.590 --> 01:59:56.923
Then you are a torturer.

01:59:58.261 --> 01:59:59.696
For God's sake.

02:00:00.196 --> 02:00:01.092
Sir.

02:00:02.563 --> 02:00:04.538
I cannot imagine what
hatred has been in your heart

02:00:04.673 --> 02:00:06.565
for you to allow this, but
I will not have you near her.

02:00:06.699 --> 02:00:08.540
Get out. Now. Go.

02:00:09.404 --> 02:00:10.942
Go!

02:00:11.079 --> 02:00:12.602
Where's the doctor?

02:00:12.738 --> 02:00:13.841
No, no.

02:00:15.845 --> 02:00:18.681
No, don't go.
Please, Nelly.

02:00:25.993 --> 02:00:27.217
I think I must.

02:00:28.094 --> 02:00:30.121
Whatever it was,

02:00:31.694 --> 02:00:33.729
I'm sure you did not mean it.

02:00:34.967 --> 02:00:35.995
Oh...

02:00:38.138 --> 02:00:40.070
But I think I did.

02:00:45.408 --> 02:00:46.611
I won't tell.

02:00:49.545 --> 02:00:50.647
I won't tell.

02:00:55.922 --> 02:00:56.951
Nelly...

02:00:57.550 --> 02:00:58.590
Yes?

02:02:09.191 --> 02:02:13.533
Heathcliff... Heathcliff...

02:02:14.994 --> 02:02:16.967
I said you would kill me.

02:02:17.103 --> 02:02:18.037
Look.

02:02:19.833 --> 02:02:21.968
No, no, no.

02:02:22.103 --> 02:02:24.008
No, you will be well
by tomorrow.

02:02:24.144 --> 02:02:26.472
Hmm? Hmm?

02:02:26.606 --> 02:02:30.208
Think of the number of times
you have claimed to be dying.

02:02:30.877 --> 02:02:32.383
Thousands at least.

02:02:35.652 --> 02:02:37.183
I've never believed you.

02:02:38.686 --> 02:02:40.251
And I won't today.

02:02:42.526 --> 02:02:44.058
 You are fine.

02:02:46.058 --> 02:02:47.398
 You will be fine.

02:04:36.276 --> 02:04:37.841
I'm sorry.

02:04:44.485 --> 02:04:46.147
Get off me. I'll kill you.

02:04:52.327 --> 02:04:53.758
Heathcliff, do not.

02:04:56.463 --> 02:04:57.993
You do not want to see...

02:06:04.430 --> 02:06:06.491
Oh, no.

02:06:08.631 --> 02:06:10.296
No, no, no.

02:07:05.184 --> 02:07:06.652
Heathcliff...

02:07:06.788 --> 02:07:07.826
What?

02:07:08.824 --> 02:07:10.895
Cathy? Cathy?

02:07:12.860 --> 02:07:13.899
Wha...

02:07:18.001 --> 02:07:19.470
Get the doctor!
For God's sake,

02:07:19.605 --> 02:07:21.108
somebody get the doctor!

02:07:23.945 --> 02:07:26.978
You are all right.
You are fine.

02:07:28.415 --> 02:07:31.612
My love, my love.

02:07:31.748 --> 02:07:33.346
My darling pain.

02:07:37.019 --> 02:07:40.618
Only do not go. No.

02:07:42.960 --> 02:07:44.864
No, no, do not go.

02:07:45.499 --> 02:07:46.866
It is unutterable.

02:07:50.067 --> 02:07:52.431
I cannot live without my life.

02:07:53.740 --> 02:07:55.775
I cannot live without my soul.

02:07:57.844 --> 02:08:00.407
You... You said I killed you.

02:08:02.476 --> 02:08:04.950
Haunt me then.

02:08:07.312 --> 02:08:08.921
Be with me always.

02:08:10.854 --> 02:08:12.418
Take any form.

02:08:15.694 --> 02:08:17.258
Drive me mad.

02:08:29.973 --> 02:08:32.107
Only please do not leave me

02:08:32.242 --> 02:08:34.781
in this abyss
where I cannot find you.

02:08:42.053 --> 02:08:43.351
 Heathcliff...

02:08:45.988 --> 02:08:47.025
 I'm sorry.

02:08:50.596 --> 02:08:51.765
Don't be sorry.

02:08:54.362 --> 02:08:56.902
Don't ever be sorry
for me, Cathy.

02:08:57.038 --> 02:09:00.471
 For I would do it
 again and again.

02:09:02.878 --> 02:09:04.306
 Then we're doomed.

02:09:09.945 --> 02:09:11.049
 What can I do?

02:09:11.884 --> 02:09:12.918
 Nothing.

02:09:15.413 --> 02:09:16.856
 Just stay with me.

02:09:29.427 --> 02:09:30.463
 Cathy?

02:09:34.610 --> 02:09:36.173
 Cathy, are you awake?

02:09:39.610 --> 02:09:40.639
Cathy?

02:09:53.924 --> 02:09:55.125
Catherine Earnshaw...

02:09:57.790 --> 02:09:59.999
I will love you
until the day that I die...

02:10:03.472 --> 02:10:04.970
and forever after.
